ng or First \nWritten Warning, they will receive a Final Written Warning. \n● For 15 points and above, they may receive an NTE for Suspension or \nAdministrative Hearing without prior warnings.\nATTENDANCE POINT SYSTEM (APS) \nAddendum (as of March 20, 2024)\nII. Second Administrative Hearing Protocol:\nAfter the first administrative hearing, the accumulation of another 3 points \nfollowing the notice of decision will subject the individual to a second \nadministrative hearing. This information will also be included in the Notice of \nDecision.\nIII. Clarification on Critical-Work Day (CWD) Sanction:\nFor CWD, if the manager requests to apply this sanction based on the \nhandbook, the employee\'s APS points will not be marked as CWD. If the APS \npoints are marked as CWD, no separate NTE will be sent to the employee.\nATTENDANCE POINT SYSTEM (APS) \nAddendum (as of March 20, 2024)\nIV. Handling \'Getting 3 Sanctions within 6 Months:\nThis provision applies to individuals experiencing attendance issues over a 6-month \nperiod without showing improvement. Due to the fluctuation of points within a certain \nprogression level, employees are subject to receive a suspension NTE for Gross and \nHabitual offenses.\nSample for fluctuating equal to or more than 3 \npoints, which is subject to repetitive verbal \nwarning:\nAttendance\nFinal Points\nJan 16 - Absent + 3 points\n3\nFeb 15 - Rollback - 1 point\n2\nFeb 16 - Absent + 3 points\n5\nApril 17 - Rollback - 4 points\n1\nApr 18 - Absent + 3 points\n4\nJun 18 - Rollback - 4 points\n0\nJun 19 - Absent + 3 points\n3\nATTENDANCE POINT SYSTEM (APS) \nAddendum (as of March 20, 2024)\nV. Validity of NTEs:\nThe validity of NTEs varies based on the type: NODs for Verbal Warnings, First \nWritten Warnings, and Final Written Warnings will be void if no additional points are \naccumulated within six (6) months. NODs for Suspensions and Administrative \nHearings will expire after twelve (12) months or if points reset back to 0 after rollback, \nwhichever comes first.\nVI. NTE Issuance and Progression:\nFor points that do not accumulate within 60 days and have not resulted in any NTEs, \nwe are not permitted to issue an NTE beyond this period. Another NTE can only be \nissued if another point is accrued. Depending on the number of points accrued, we \nmay skip a progression step and issue a Final Written Warning, Suspension, or \nAdministrative Hearing immediately. However, special cases may arise where \nsuspension dates are scheduled based on the Operations\' requirements.\nATTENDANCE POINT SYSTEM (APS) \nAddendum (Effective: April 14, 2025)\nII. Critical Work Day Policy\nUsage of Sick Leave credits on Critical Work Days will require an approved \nmedical certificate or supporting documents, regardless of whether it is a single \nor multiple-day absence.\nIII. Exclusion of LOA/ML/MedLOA for Rollback Days\n● Employees on Leave of Absence (LOA), Maternity Leave (ML), or Medical \nLeave of Absence (MedLOA) will not have rollback days deducted from their \nattendance records.\n● The rollback day count will be paused during the period of \nLOA/ML/MedLOA and will resume once the employee is back on duty.\nATTENDANCE POINT SYSTEM (APS) \nAddendum (Effective: April 14, 2025)\nIV. Limited Acceptance of APS Waiver Documents\n● Employees must submit supporting documents within 5 calendar days \nfrom the issuance of the Notice to Explain (NTE) to be considered for APS \nwaiver.\n● Documents submitted after the issuance of the Notice of Decision (NOD) \nwill not be accepted. This rule will be strictly implemented without \nexceptions.\nATTENDANCE POINT SYSTEM (APS) \nAddendum (Effective: April 14, 2025)\nV. Accepted Documents for APS Waiver \nOnly the following documents will be accepted for waiving APS points:\n● Medical documents of the employee/medical documents of an immediate \nfamily member (proof of hospitalization, medical emergency, or death).\n● Government-related documents (e.g., police reports, court summons, or any \nlegal document requiring the employee’s presence).\n● Other emergency-related documents that clearly explain the cause of \nabsence, subject to RTA/Management approval.\nATTENDANCE POINT SYSTEM (APS) \nAddendum (Effective: April 14, 2025)\nVI. Non-Accepted Documents for APS Waiver\nThe following documents will not be accepted as they do not fall under \nemergency situations:\n● Flight or travel details\n● School-related documents (e.g., exams, school activities, or any academic \ncommitments)\n\n🗯️ Leave Requests/Process\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for  \nWalmart Support | RTA\nVacation/Sick Leave\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n| Vacation and Sick Leave Process \nPurpose/ Scope \nThis SOP establishes the standardized process for the application, approval, \nusage, accrual, and recording of Vacation Leave (VL). It ensures consistent \nimplementation of company policy while balancing employee benefits and operational \nrequirements. This SOP applies to all eligible employees and to RTA, supervisors and \nmanagers involved in Vacation Leave processing. \nDefinition of Terms \nVacation Leave (VL) – A company-initiated benefit granting eligible \nemployees paid time off based on accrued leave credits. \nHalf-Day Leave – A company-initiated benefit equivalent to four (4) or \nfive (5) continuous hours, depending on work schedule, chargeable against \navailable sick leave or vacation leave credits. \nCritical Workdays – Specific dates where leave approval is subject to \nstricter review due to operational impact. \nSick Leave (SL) - Time off granted to an employee due to illness or \nmedical reasons. \nTerminal Leave – Use of accrued VL credits prior to separation from \nemployment. \n \nRoles & Responsibilities \nList the key roles involved. \nEmployee \n●​ File VL application within prescribed timelines \n●​ Ensure completeness and accuracy of request \nSupport/Senior TL/Managers \n●​ Validate \nexceptions \nand \nApprove \nVL \nrequests \nof \nmanagerial/supervisorial employees\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \nRTA \n●​ Review and approve/disapprove VL requests \n \nVacation Leave Eligibility & Entitlement \n● ​\nRegular employees who have completed at least twelve (12) \ncontinuous months of service are entitled to one hundred (100) hours of paid \nVacation Leave annually. \n● ​\nFor new hires, VL accrues starting from the hiring date and may be \nused upon regularization. \n● ​\nEmployees with perfect attendance and zero tardiness for the \nentire calendar year are granted an additional twenty (20) hours VL credits for \nthe succeeding year. These credits are non-convertible to cash if unused. \n \nProcedure (Steps) \nStep 1: Filing of Leave Application \n● ​\nThe employee must file a Vacation/Sick Leave application through the \nZoho Leave Application Form. \nA.​ Filing a Vacation Leave Request \n●​ Agents must file their VL request in Zoho. \n●​ The agent must consider filing in accordance with the criteria. \nB.​ Filing a Sick Leave Request \n●​ Agents must file their SL request in Zoho immediately after \nreturning from an absence. \n●​ If the SL request covers less than 2 days, no additional documents \nare required. \nC.​ Documentation Requirements for Extended Absences \n●​ If the absence is 2 days or more, agents are required to submit: \n○​ A medical certificate from a licensed doctor. \n○​ A fit-to-work validation confirming their ability to resume \nduties.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \nStep 2: Review Employee Request \n● ​\nThe RTA reviews the request based on staffing and operational \nneeds. This is in accordance with the availability of slots on that date and also if \nthe filed date under the date-range.  \nCriteria for Vacation Leave Approval;​\n​\n1. Filed requests must be submitted at least thirty (30) in advance \nor seven (7) calendar days prior to the intended leave date. \n2. There must be an available slot for that day for it to be approved.  \n● ​\nManagerial or Supervisorial employees must secure approval from \nTop Management (STL/OM) \n● ​\nLeave applications without proper approval shall be considered \ndisapproved, unauthorized, or AWOL. \nStep 3: Approving of Employee Request \nAccess Leave Request. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nStep 3.1.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \nIn the Zoho Leave Request Portal, locate the left-side navigation panel. \n1.​ Find the tab labeled “View” and click on it. \n2.​ From the dropdown menu, select “Leaves for Approval”. \n3.​ This section will display a list of all pending leave requests submitted by \nemployees. \n \nNote: If you cannot view a certain program/account, please reach out to your RTA \nleader to request for the access/approver’s view of the program/account. \nStep 3.2. \nIn the Leaves for Approval section, you will see the following details: \na.​ Employee Name \nb.​ Type of Leave (Sick Leave, Vacation Leave, Bereavement Leave, etc.) \nc.​ Date Range of the Leave \nd.​ Leave Reason (if provided by the employee) \ne.​ Current Status (Pending, Approved, or Disapproved) \nClick on an employee’s request to view additional details.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \nIf necessary, cross-check the employee’s attendance records in Zoho Time \nLogs to verify leave eligibility. \nStep 3.3. \n1.​ To Approve a Leave Request: \n○​ Click the \"Approve\" button next to the request if the request is compliant \nto the criteria above. \n○​ The system will automatically update the leave status to \"Approved\" and \nnotify the employee. \n2.​ To Disapprove a Leave Request: \n○​ Click the \"Disapprove\" button. \n○​ A pop-up window will appear, prompting you to enter the reason for \ndisapproval. \n○​ Type in a clear and specific reason (e.g., “Your request falls within the \nfiling date range”, “There are no remaining slots available” or “Schedule \nconflict”). \n○​ Click \"Confirm\" to finalize the disapproval. \n○​ The employee will receive an automated notification regarding the \ndisapproval along with the reason provided. \nLeave Utilization \n● ​\nApproved VL is deducted from the employee’s available VL credits. \n● ​\nEmployees under suspension are not allowed to apply or use VL \ncredits. \n \nSpecial Vacation Leave Scenarios \n \n●​ Birthday Leave Request \n○​ Support Employees are eligible for Birthday Leave. This leave follows the \nsame request process as regular leave; however, it may only be filed for \nany one day within the employee’s birth month. Birthday Leave is limited \nto one (1) day only. \n●​ Emergency Vacation Leave \n○​ Employees may be granted spontaneous leave subject to approval by \nthe Operations Team and higher authority. This leave follows the regular\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \nfiling process but may be approved even if standard criteria are not fully \nmet, typically for urgent situations such as medical emergencies affecting \nthe employee or their immediate family, with required approval and \nsupporting documentation. \n●​ Voluntary Time-off Leave filing \n○​ This follows the same process as regular leave filing but applies to \nVoluntary Time-Off (VTO). VTO is unpaid and will be deducted from the \ncutoff date of the leave. It may only be requested if the employee has no \navailable leave credits, and it requires approval from the Operations Team. \n \n \nYear-End and Carryover Rules \n● ​\nAll VL credits for the current year must be used on or before the end of \nthe first quarter of the succeeding year. \n● ​\nUnused VL beyond this period shall be converted into cash. \n \nSeparation and Proration \n● ​\nFor outgoing employees, VL accrual is prorated based on active \nemployment. \n● ​\nAny VL taken in excess of prorated credits shall be deducted from final \npay. \n● ​\nFor separated or terminated employees for just or authorized cause, VL is \nnot convertible to cash. \n \nReprocessing Previously Denied Leave Requests \n​\nHere is the guide for reprocessing previously denied leave requests. Please \nreview and follow the steps accordingly: Guided Standard Operating Procedure for \nReprocessing Previously Denied Leave Requests.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \nExceptions & Escalation \n●​ VL applications without proper approval are considered unauthorized. \n●​ Employees under suspension are ineligible to use VL credits. \n●​ Management decisions related to VL scheduling are final and binding. \nReferences \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Workforce Real-Time Analyst (RTA)_020…\n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Workforce Real-Time Analyst (RTA)_020…\n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Workforce Real-Time Analyst (RTA)_020…\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \n \n \n \nSTANDARD OPERATING PROCEDURE (SOP) \nSOP INFORMATION \nField                                                                       ​\nDetails \nSOP Title:                                                              ​\nVacation/Sick Leave \nDepartment / Team:                                            ​\nAgent View \n \n \n1. Purpose / Scope \nThis SOP outlines the process for filing and managing Vacation Leave (VL) \nrequests. It applies to all employees who need to request VL and covers the steps from \nsubmitting the application to awaiting approval from the RTA Team. \n \n2. Roles & Responsibilities \nRole​ ​\n​\nResponsibility \nEmployee​\n​\nSubmit VL requests accurately and provide required information. \nRTA Team​\n​\nReview, approve, or deny VL requests and update the status in the  \nsystem. \n​\n​\n3. Tools / Requirements \nZoho Leave Application Form\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \nAccess to the employee portal / leave system \n \n4. Procedure (Steps) \nStep 1: Filing of Vacation Leave Application \n● ​\nThe employee must file a VL application through the Zoho Leave \nApplication Form. \n \nStep 2: Fill up the form \n \nFill in the necessary information: \n●​ Name: Already filled \n●​ From: Start date of the VL request \n●​ To: End date of the VL request \n●​ Status: VL in hours/SL in Hours \nAdditional Information:\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \n​\n​\n \n●​ Reason: Reason for the leave \n●​ Remark: Optional – can be left blank or include additional details \nregarding the VL \nNote: Sick Leave (SL) cannot be filed in advance. All SL requests must be \nsubmitted on the employee’s return or reporting day. \n \nStep 3: Wait for the Decision \nYou can check the status of your leave request here and wait for the RTA Team \nto make a decision. \n \n \nNotes / Tips:\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \n●​ Ensure all dates and information are accurate to avoid delays. \n●​ Keep a record of your request for reference. \n \n5. Exceptions & Escalation \nIssue \nAction \nEscalate To \nLeave request not \nshowing \nRefresh portal and confirm \nsubmission \nRTA Team \nIncorrect VL details \nSubmit correction or update request \nTeam Lead/RTA\nBereavement Leave\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n| Bereavement Process \nPurpose/ Scope \nThis SOP defines the standardized process for requesting, validating, approving, \nand recording Bereavement Leave. It applies to all employees, regardless of \nemployment status, and to HR personnel and RTAs responsible for approving and \nprocessing Bereavement Leave requests in Zoho. The SOP ensures timely employee \nsupport while maintaining accurate documentation and compliance with company policy. \n \nRoles & Responsibilities \nList the key roles involved. \n Employee \n●​ Notify HR Department of \nbereavement \n●​ Submit required documents \n●​ File leave request within the \nprescribed period \nImmediate Supervisor / Team \nLead \n●​ Acknowledge employee \nabsence \n●​ Support coordination with \nHR Department if needed \nHuman Resources Department \n(HRD) \n●​ Validate documents \n●​ Approve and record \nBereavement Leave \nRTA \n●​ Approves request on Zoho based \non the approval of Ops and HR \n \nProcedure (Steps) \nStep 1: Employee Notification \n● The employee must inform HRD and/or their immediate supervisor as soon as \nreasonably possible regarding the bereavement.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \n● Notification may be done via email, or other company-approved communication \nchannels. \nStep 2: Submission of Bereavement Leave Request \n● The employee completes and submits the Zoho Leave Application Form. \n● The requested leave may cover up to three (3) working days. \n● Filing all the documents needed in Zoho \nStep 3: Submission of Supporting Documents \n● The employee submits the following documents to HRD via Email: \n○ Copy of the death certificate \n○ Proof of relationship with the deceased (if required) \nStep 4: HRD Review and Validation \n● HRD reviews the request form and validates the submitted documents. \n● HRD confirms eligibility based on the definition of an immediate family member. \n● HRD then approves the Bereavement leave thru email and so for the RTA to \napprove it in Zoho \nStep 5: Approval and Recording \n● Once validated, HRD approves the Bereavement Leave. \n● The leave is recorded as Bereavement Leave, separate from vacation and \nsick leave credits. \n \nReview Employee Request \n● The RTA reviews the request based upon prior approval of the HRD. \nCriteria;​\n​\n1. Requests must be approved by the HRD via email.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \n2. The request is acknowledged by the operations team. \n● Managerial or Supervisorial employees must secure approval from Top \nManagement (STL/OM) \n● Leave applications without proper approval shall be considered disapproved, \nunauthorized, or AWOL. \nA.​ Approving of Employee Request \nAccess Leave Request. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nB.​ In the Zoho Leave Request Portal, locate the left-side navigation panel. \nI.​\nFind the tab labeled “View” and click on it. \nII.​\nFrom the dropdown menu, select “Leaves for Approval”. \nIII.​\nThis section will display a list of all pending leave requests submitted by \nemployees.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \n \nNote: If you cannot view a certain program/account, please reach out to your RTA \nleader to request for the access/approver’s view of the program/account. \nC. In the Leaves for Approval section, you will see the following details: \na.​ Employee Name \nb.​ Type of Leave (Sick Leave, Vacation Leave, Bereavement Leave, etc.) \nc.​ Date Range of the Leave \nd.​ Leave Reason (if provided by the employee) \ne.​ Current Status (Pending, Approved, or Disapproved) \nClick on an employee’s request to view additional details. \nIf necessary, cross-check the employee’s attendance records in Zoho Time \nLogs to verify leave eligibility. \nD. Approval of the request \n1.​ To Approve a Leave Request: \n○​ Click the \"Approve\" button next to the request if the request is compliant \nto the criteria above.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \n○​ The system will automatically update the leave status to \"Approved\" and \nnotify the employee. \n2.​ To Disapprove a Leave Request: \n○​ Click the \"Disapprove\" button. \n○​ A pop-up window will appear, prompting you to enter the reason for \ndisapproval. \n○​ Type in a clear and specific reason (e.g., “Your request falls within the \nfiling date range”, “There are no remaining slots available” or “Schedule \nconflict”). \n○​ Click \"Confirm\" to finalize the disapproval. \n○​ The employee will receive an automated notification regarding the \ndisapproval along with the reason provided. \n \nExceptions & Escalation \n●​ Failure to submit required documents may result in the leave being reclassified \naccording to company leave policies. \n \nReferences \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Workforce Real-Time Analyst (RTA)_020…\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \n \n \n \nSTANDARD OPERATING PROCEDURE (SOP) \nSOP INFORMATION \nField                                                                       ​\nDetails \nSOP Title:                                                              ​\nBereavement Leave \nDepartment / Team:                                            ​\nAgent View \n \n \n 1. Purpose / Scope \nThis SOP outlines the process for filing a Bereavement Leave (BL) request through \nZoho Attendance. It applies to all employees requesting BL due to the passing of an \nimmediate family member and covers filing, documentation requirements, submission, \nand retraction procedures. \n \n2. Roles & Responsibilities \nRole \nResponsibility \nEmployee \nFile the BL request accurately and upload the required \nsupporting document. \nRTA Team \nReview submitted BL requests, validate documents, and \napprove or deny the request.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \n \n3. Tools / Requirements \n●​ Zoho Attendance / Leave Request Page​\n \n●​ Scanned or clear image of a Death Certificate or Embalming Certificate​\n \n●​ Document must be stamped and processed by the Local Civil Registry Office \n(LCRO)​\n \n \n4. Procedure (Steps) \nStep 1: Access the Leave Request Page \n●​ Log in to Zoho Attendance and navigate to the Leave Request page. \n \nStep 2: Select Bereavement Leave Dates \n●​ Enter the dates to be availed for Bereavement Leave. \n●​ Ensure that the date range does not exceed three (3) days.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \n●​ A pop-up reminder will appear prompting you to upload the required supporting \ndocument. \n \nStep 3: Fill in the Required Details \n●​ Status: BL (Bereavement Leave – not Birthday Leave) \n●​ Relation: Relationship to the deceased \n●​ Reason: Bereavement Leave \n●​ Remarks: Optional notes or additional information, if applicable \n​\n \nStep 4: Upload Supporting Document (any \nof the following) \n●​ Click Upload Supporting Document. \n○​ Attach a Death Certificate with \nan official stamp. \nNote: Uploading any other document \n(including images of the deceased) will result \nin automatic disapproval.​\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \n \n \n \n \nStep 5: Submit the Request \n●​ Once the document is uploaded, click \nSubmit. \n●​ Your Bereavement Leave request will be \nofficially filed. \nStep 6: Leave Retraction (If Needed) \n●​ Go to My Records > My Attendance. \n●​ Click Retract Leave and inform an RTA to review and approve the retraction.​\n \nNotes / Tips: \n●​ Ensure documents are clear and complete before uploading.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \n●​ Incorrect or missing documents will delay or result in denial of the request.​\n \n \n \n \n5. Exceptions & Escalation \nIssue \nAction \nEscalate To \nIncorrect document \nuploaded \nRetract and refile the \nrequest \nRTA Team \nRequest auto-denied \nVerify document and refile \nRTA Team \nRetraction not approved \nFollow up via proper \nchannel \nRTA / \nSupervisor\nSolo Parent Leave\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n| Solo Parent Leave Process \nPurpose / Scope \nThis SOP establishes the standardized process for the application, approval, validation, \nand recording of Parental Leave (Solo Parent Leave). It ensures compliance with applicable \nlaws and company policy while providing eligible solo parent employees time off to perform \nparental duties that require their physical presence. This applies to all eligible solo parent \nemployees and to RTA, HRD, supervisors, managers, and payroll personnel involved in leave \nprocessing. \n \nDefinition of Terms \nParental Leave (Solo Parent Leave) – A leave benefit of up to seven (7) working days per \nyear granted to an eligible solo parent employee to enable the performance of parental duties \nand responsibilities where physical presence is required. \nSolo Parent – Any individual who is solely responsible for the care and upbringing of a child or \nchildren and falls under the categories defined in Section 5 of this SOP. \n \nRoles & Responsibilities \nRole \n               Responsibility \nEmployee (Solo \nParent) \n• Inform HRD and Support Team of solo parent \neligibility \n• Submit Parental Leave application and documents \n• Report any change in eligibility status \nImmediate Supervisor \n• Review and approve/disapprove leave requests \nHuman Resources \nDepartment (HRD)/ \nReal Time Analyst \n• Validate eligibility and documents \n• Maintain records of Solo Parent status\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nTools / Forms Required \n●​ Zoho Leave Application Form (Parental Leave option) \n●​ Valid Solo Parent Eligibility Identification Card issued by DSWD \n●​ Supporting documents, if applicable \n \nEligibility Criteria \nEmployment Requirement \n●​ Parental Leave of not more than seven (7) working days per year shall be \ngranted to any solo parent employee who has rendered at least six (6) months \nof service. \nDefinition of Solo Parent \nA solo parent includes, but is not limited to, the following: \n●​ A woman who gives birth as a result of rape or other crimes against chastity, \nprovided the mother keeps and raises the child; \n●​ A parent left solo due to the death of a spouse; \n●​ A parent left solo due to the detention or imprisonment of a spouse for at least \none (1) year; \n●​ A parent left solo due to physical and/or mental incapacity of the spouse, as \ncertified by a public medical practitioner; \n●​ A parent left solo due to legal separation or de facto separation from spouse \nfor at least one (1) year, provided custody of the child is awarded to the \nemployee; \n●​ A parent left solo due to nullity or annulment of marriage, as decreed by a \ncourt or church, provided custody of the child is awarded to the employee; \n●​ A parent left solo due to abandonment by the spouse for at least one (1) year; \n●​ An unmarried mother or father who chooses to keep and rear the child; \n●​ A duly licensed foster parent or court-appointed legal guardian who solely \nprovides parental care; \n●​ Any family member who assumes responsibility as head of the family due to \ndeath, abandonment, disappearance, or prolonged absence of the parents or \nsolo parent.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nProof of Eligibility \n●​ Employees must possess a valid Solo Parent Eligibility Identification Card \nissued by the Department of Social Welfare and Development (DSWD). \n●​ HRD and RTAmust be formally informed once eligibility is granted. \n \nProcedure (Steps) \nStep 1: Declaration of Solo Parent Status \n●​ The employee informs HRD and RTA of solo parent eligibility and submits a copy of the \nvalid DSWD-issued Solo Parent ID. \nStep 2: Filing of Parental Leave Application \n●​ Employee submits Parental Leave request via the Zoho Leave Application Form. \n●​ Requests must follow standard leave filing timelines unless otherwise approved by \nManagement. \nStep 3: Supervisor Review and Approval \n●​ Immediate Supervisor reviews the request based on operational needs and approves or \ndisapproves the leave. \nStep 4: HRD and RTA Validation \n●​ HRD and RTA verifies eligibility, remaining Parental Leave balance, and document \nvalidity. \nStep 5: Recording and Payroll Coordination \n●​ Approved Parental Leave is recorded as paid leave. \n●​ Payroll ensures the leave is not converted to cash and is properly reflected in \nattendance records. \nChange in Eligibility Status \n●​ Any change in the employee’s status or circumstance that removes solo parent \nresponsibility must be immediately reported to HRD and RTA\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n●​ Failure to disclose such changes may result in corrective action up to and including \ntermination, depending on the circumstances. \n●​ Upon loss of eligibility, Parental Leave benefits shall cease. \n \nSpecial Rules / Exceptions \n●​ Parental Leave is not convertible to cash and cannot be carried over. \n●​ Unused Parental Leave credits are forfeited at year-end. \n●​ Management reserves the right to validate eligibility at any time. \n \nRecords / Outputs \n●​ Approved Parental Leave Applications \n●​ Copy of DSWD-issued Solo Parent ID \n●​ Updated employee leave records \nReference \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Workforce Real-Time Analyst (RTA)_020…\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/\nRetraction Process\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n| Retraction Process \nPurpose / Scope \nThis SOP provides employees with clear instructions on how to properly request a \nretraction using the Zoho. It ensures accurate workforce planning, avoids scheduling conflicts, \nand prevents unauthorized schedule changes. This applies to all employees who need to retract \nan already submitted and approved leave request. \n \nDefinition of Terms \nLeave Retraction – A request submitted by an employee to cancel or withdraw a \npreviously filed leave request that has not yet been taken. \nZoho Leave System – The company-approved platform used for filing, approving, and \nmanaging leave requests. \n \nEmployee Responsibilities \nEmployees requesting leave retraction must: \n●​ Submit the retraction request promptly and correctly \n●​ Ensure the leave has not yet been taken \n●​ Monitor the request status for approval or denial \n●​ Continue to follow the original approved schedule until the retraction is approved \n \nProcedure – How to Submit a Leave Retraction Request\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \n●​ Open a supported web browser (Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, or Microsoft Edge). \n●​ Navigate to the ECETrack / Zoho Leave System using the company-provided URL. \n●​ Log in using your company credentials. \nStep 1: Locate Your Leave Request \n●​ Go to the Leave Requests or My Leaves section. \n●​ Identify the leave request you want to retract. \nStep 2: Submit the Leave Retraction  \n●​ Select the option to Retract, Cancel, or Withdraw the leave (depending on system \nlabeling). \n●​ Provide a clear and valid reason for the retraction (e.g., change in plans, operational \nneed). \n●​ Submit the retraction request.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStep 3: Wait for Approval Decision  \n●​ Once the retraction request has been submitted in the Zoho, the employee should notify \nthe available RTA for them to review the request. \n●​ Do not assume the retraction is approved until you receive system confirmation. \n \nImportant Rules and Reminders \n●​ Leave retractions are subject to approval and are not automatic. \n●​ Retraction only applies 24 hours before the filed date of leave. \n●​ Retraction requests may be denied if: \n○​ The leave has already been taken \n○​ Workforce coverage will be negatively impacted \n○​ There are scheduling conflicts \n●​ Employees must continue to follow the original approved leave schedule until the \nretraction is officially approved. \n●​ Unauthorized schedule changes without approved retraction may result in attendance \nor payroll issues. \n \nNotifications and Status Updates \n●​ Once a decision is made: \n○​ Approved retractions will automatically remove the leave from records. \n○​ Denied retractions will include a reason for denial. \n●​ Employees will receive automated notifications via the Zoho system. \n \nTechnical Issues and Support \n●​ If you experience technical issues accessing the Zoho Leave System: \n○​ Report the issue immediately to the IT Support Team. \n○​ Inform your Immediate Supervisor if the issue affects your schedule.\nLactation Breaks Guidelines\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n| Lactation Break Process \nPurpose / Scope \nThis SOP outlines the process for availing lactation breaks for breastfeeding \nemployees. It applies to eligible nursing mothers and covers entitlement, proper usage, \ndocumentation, and compliance with company policy and labor regulations. \n \nRoles & Responsibilities \nRole \nResponsibility \nEmployee \nAvail lactation breaks responsibly, follow scheduling guidelines, \nand complete required documentation. \nCompany Nurse \nValidate lactation breaks and sign the Lactation Form. \nRTA / Operations \nTeam \nMonitor adherence to break limits and ensure proper recording. \n \nTools / Requirements \n●​ Lactation Form \n \nProcedure (Steps) \nStep 1: Determine Lactation Break Eligibility \n●​ Breastfeeding employees are entitled to 5 minutes of lactation break per working \nhour. \n●​ Accumulated break time is as follows:​\n \n○​ 8-hour shift: 40 minutes​\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n○​ 10-hour shift: 50 minutes​\n \nStep 2: Schedule Lactation Breaks \n●​ Lactation breaks must be taken within the clinic or at home for Work-from-Home \n(WFH) employees to ensure a safe and comfortable environment. \n●​ The total lactation break time must not be taken all at once and should be divided \ninto 2–3 milk expression sessions. \nStep 3: Record Lactation Breaks \n●​ Complete the Lactation Form accurately for each lactation break taken. \n●​ Ensure the form is validated and signed by the Company Nurse for \ndocumentation and compliance.​\n \nStep 4: Observe Time Limits and Duration \n●​ Lactation breaks may be availed for up to six (6) months from eligibility.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n●​ Exceeding the allowed lactation break time will be considered an overbreak and \nthe excess time will be deducted from salary.​\n \nNotes / Tips: \n●​ Proper scheduling helps avoid workflow disruption. \n●​ Always ensure documentation is complete and validated on the same day.​\n \n \nExceptions & Escalation \nIssue \nAction \nEscalate To \nExceeded allowed lactation \ntime \nReview break usage and record \noverbreak \nRTA / Operations \nTeam \nMissing \nor \nunsigned \nLactation Form \nCoordinate \nvalidation \nimmediately \nCompany Nurse \nClinic access issues \nReport and seek guidance \nOperations Team \n \nQuality Check / Expected Result \n●​ Lactation breaks are taken within the allowed time and location. \n●​ The lactation form is properly completed and signed by the Company Nurse. \n●​ No unauthorized overbreaks are recorded, ensuring compliance with policy.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/\nOvertime (OT) Request/Process\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n| Overtime Request Process \nPurpose/Scope \n \nTo define the standard process for requesting, approving, and documenting overtime \nwork to ensure operational needs are met while maintaining compliance with company \npolicies.This applies to all supports and agents. \n \nDefinitions \n●​ Pre-Shift OT – Overtime rendered before the agent’s scheduled shift start. \n●​ Post-Shift OT – Overtime rendered after the agent’s scheduled shift end. \n●​ OT Commitment Form – Required form confirming the agent’s availability \nand agreement to render OT. \n \nGeneral Guidelines \n​\n(RDOT, Pre-Shift & Post-Shift) \n1.​ Pre-Approval: All overtime must be requested and approved before the work is \nperformed, except in emergency cases. \n2.​ Deadlines: Requests must be submitted within 24 hours of the overtime worked if \npre-approval was verbal. \n3.​ Rendering overtime without prior approval is not allowed. \n4.​ OT requests may be denied due to staffing sufficiency, budget limits, or \nperformance considerations. \n5.​ Approval is subject to operational demand. \n \n \nProcedure Steps \n \nStep 1: Filling an OT Confirmation Form \nLogin: Access your Zoho OT Commitment Form, an Overtime \n(OT) Commitment Form is typically used to document an \nemployee\'s agreement to work extra hours, ensuring compliance \nwith labor laws.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nLogin to Zoho Creator/ECETrack. On the navigation bar, go to OT Tab. Then, \nselect OT Commitment Form. \n \n   Note: The OT Commitment Form must be fully completed prior to the scheduled \nRDOT shift date. \n \nStep 2: Fill up the necessary information \nEmployee details (Name, Lunch, Site, Account, ID) are sometimes auto-populated by \nthe system. \nFill Details: \n○​ Date: Select the date the OT will occur. \n○​ Time Limit: Specify the number of hours (2 hours). \n○​ Start Time: The time OT is scheduled to begin. \n○​ End Time: Auto-calculated based on Start Time + Time Limit; not editable \nto prevent errors. \n○​ Notes/Remarks: Briefly state the project or task requiring extra time \n(urgent deliverable, system downtime recovery, etc.).\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n○​ Agreement Checkbox:  Employee must tick this to acknowledge that OT is \nvoluntary and subject to RTA approval. \n○​ Submit: Click Submit. \n \nStep 3: View Your Filed OT Requests \n●​ After submission, go to the My OT Commitments tab. \n●​ Here, you can track the status of your request: \n \n○​ Pending: Awaiting RTA review. \n○​ Approved: OT is confirmed. \n○​ Disapproved: OT request has been declined. \n \nStep 4: Coordination with WFM / RTA \n●​ Coordinate with WFM/RTA for:​\n \n○​ Final validation \n○​ OT plotting in the system \n●​ Ensure agents are informed of final approval status. \n \n \nRest Day Overtime (RDOT) Request \n \nRDOT (Rest Day Overtime): Overtime rendered on an agent’s officially \nscheduled rest day, subject to prior approval. \n \n​\n \nStep 1: Access the official RDOT Request Form/System (Zoho).​\n \nStep 2: Specific Details: Fill up the necessary fields. \n \n \nA.​ Name: Sometimes auto-populated by the system. \nB.​ Date: Select the correct Shift Date. \nC.​ Overtime Type: Select \"Rest Day\" from the \ndropdown (if configured). \nD.​ Timing: Enter the “Start time” (23:00 PM) and \n\"End time” (10:00 AM).\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nE.​ Number of Hours: This will auto-calculate based on the Start Time and Time \nLimit. \nF.​ Reason: Detail the specific task or reason for rendering OT (System deployment \nrequired before staff arrival or Pre-meeting prep for international clients). \n \nStep 3: Submit: Click Submit. \n \n \n \nPre-shift Overtime (OT) Request \n \nPre-shift Overtime refers to any work performed prior to the employee’s officially \nscheduled shift start time. \nExample:  Starting at 7:00 AM when the shift starts at 9:00 AM \n \nPolicy Rules \n \n●​ Prior Approval: All pre-shift OT must be submitted and approved at least 12 \nhours before the start of the early work. \n●​ Productive Work: Employees must be at their workstations and actively working \nduring this period; \"commute time\" or \"early arrival for personal reasons\" does \nnot qualify. \n●​ Grace Period: Early clock-ins of less than 15 minutes are generally considered \n\"incidental\" and do not require a formal OT request unless specifically instructed. \n \n \nProcedure Steps \nSubmission \n1.​ Open Zoho Tracker: Log-in and select “Pre-shift” from the dropdown. You may \nsubmit your Pre-Shift OT request after completing your shift. \n \n \n2.​ Request Entry: Select “Home” on your \nZohoTrack Homepage, and then > OT Form.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n3.​ Specific Details: Fill up the necessary fields. \n \nA.​ Name: \nSometimes \nauto-populated by the system. \nB.​ Date: Select the correct Shift \nDate. \nC.​ Overtime Type: Select \"Regular” \nand \n“Pre-Shift\" \nfrom \nthe \ndropdown \n(if \nconfigured). \nD.​ Timing: Enter the “Start time” \n(07:00 AM) and \"End time” (09:00 AM). \nE.​ Number of Hours: This will \nauto-calculate based on the Start Time and \nTime Limit. \nF.​ Reason: Detail the specific task \nor \nreason \nfor \nrendering \nOT \n(System \ndeployment required before staff arrival or \nPre-meeting prep for international clients). \n \n4.​ Submit: Click Submit. \n \n \n●​ Overtime Execution \n○​ Employees render overtime only during the approved schedule. \n○​ Any deviation must be immediately reported to the TL or WFM. \n \n●​ Documentation and Audit \n○​ All approved OT requests must be properly documented. \n○​ Records are subject to audit and compliance review.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \n●​ Non-Compliance \n○​ Unauthorized or unapproved overtime may result in non-payment and/or \ndisciplinary action. \n○​ Repeated violations may be escalated to Operations or HR. \n \nRevision and Review \n●​ This SOP is subject to periodic review and updates based on operational or \npolicy changes. \n \nPost-shift Overtime (OT) Request \n \nPost-shift Overtime is defined as authorized work performed immediately following the \nend of an employee\'s scheduled shift. \nExample: Working until 7:00 PM when the shift ends at 5:00 PM. \n \n \nGeneral Policy \n●​ Authorization: Employees should ideally receive verbal or written (Chat/Email) clearance \nfrom their supervisor before staying late. \n●​ Minimum Duration: Only post-shift work exceeding 30 minutes or an hour qualifies for an \nOT request. \n●​ Filing Deadline: Requests must be filed in Zoho by the end of the day following the OT \nwork. \nProcedure Steps \n1.​ Open Zoho Tracker: Log-in and select “Whole Day” from the dropdown. You may submit \nyour Post-Shift OT request after completing your shift.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n2.​ Request Entry: Select “Home” on your ZohoTrack Homepage, and then > OT Form. \n \n3.​ Specific Details: Fill up the necessary fields. \nA.​ Name: Sometimes auto-populated by \nthe system. \nB.​ Date: Select the correct Shift Date. \nC.​ Overtime Type: Select \"Regular” and \n“Post-Shift\" from the dropdown (if configured). \nD.​ Timing: Enter the “Start time” (05:00 \nPM) and \"End time” (07:00 PM). \nE.​ Number of Hours: This will \nauto-calculate based on the Start Time and Time \nLimit. \nF.​ Reason: Detail the specific task or \nreason for rendering OT (Delayed server migration or \nUnscheduled client emergency call). \n \n4.​ Submit: Click Submit. \n \n●​ Cancellation or Changes \n \n○​ If you can no longer render approved OT, inform your TL immediately. \n○​ Changes to approved OT require re-approval. \n \n●​ Non-Compliance \n \n○​ Unapproved overtime may not be paid. \n○​ Repeated violations may result in disciplinary action. \n \nSupport \n \n●​ For questions or concerns about overtime requests, please contact your Team Lead or \nWFM/RTA on shift.\nSchedule Change Request\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n| Schedule Change Request \n \nPurpose/Scope \n \nTo define the standard process for requesting, reviewing, approving, and documenting \nschedule changes while ensuring operational coverage and compliance with company \npolicies. This SOP applies to all employees. \n \nTypes of Schedule Changes Covered \n \n●​ Shift time change \n●​ Swap of working days or rest days \n●​ Temporary or permanent schedule adjustment \n●​ One-time schedule modification due to operational or personal reasons \n \nGuidelines \n \n●​ All schedule change requests must be filed in advance. \n●​ Schedule changes are subject to approval based on staffing needs. \n●​ Do not follow a new schedule unless it is officially approved and communicated. \n \nHow to File a Schedule Change Request? \n \nSubmit Schedule Change Request \n \n1.​ Access the official Schedule Change Request Form/System (Zoho/ECETrack).\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n​\n​\n \n \n>>> Once you are in your My Schedule Change Request Page, Click the green plus \nsign on your upper right hand corner. \n \n \n \n2.​ Complete all required details:​\n \n○​ Full name \n○​ Requested new date schedule (FROM and TO) \n○​ Working Hours per Day (8 or 10) \n○​ New time Schedule (START and END) make sure to follow what is in the \nTransition Workbook. \n○​ Reason Note: You may add/use screenshot (imgur) \n○​ Rest Day: Just check the correct days according to the transition \nWorkbook. \n○​\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n3.​ Attach any required supporting documents, if applicable. \n \n4.​ Submit the request within the prescribed timeline. \n \n \n \nWait for Approval \n \n●​ Continue following your current schedule until approval is confirmed. \n●​ Monitor Zoho or official channels for updates. \n \nFollow Approved Schedule \n \n●​ Once approved, strictly follow the new schedule. \n●​ Any deviation must be reported immediately to your TL. \n \nCoordination with WFM / RTA \n \n●​ Endorse approved requests to WFM / RTA for validation and plotting. \n●​ Coordinate with WFM/RTA to confirm final schedule changes. \n \nCompliance and Monitoring \n \n●​ Unauthorized schedule changes are not allowed.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n●​ Non-compliance may result in attendance points or disciplinary action. \n●​ All schedule changes are subject to audit. \n \n \nSupport \n \nFor questions or clarifications: \n●​ Agents should contact their Team Lead \n●​ TLs should coordinate with WFM / RTA on shift\nAttendance Notification\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n| Submitting an Attendance Notification \nStep-by-step Guide for Submitting of Attendance Notification \nPurpose \n \nTo define the standard process for submitting, reviewing, and documenting \nattendance-related notifications in Zoho to ensure accurate tracking, proper escalation, \nand compliance with company attendance policies. This SOP applies to all employees. \n \nAttendance Notifications Covered \n \n●​ Late login \n●​ Early logout \n●​ Absence / No show \n●​ System or connectivity issues \n●​ Emergency attendance concerns​\n \nGuidelines \n \n1.​ Attendance notifications must be submitted in Zoho on the same day of \noccurrence. \n2.​ Notifications must include complete and accurate details. \n3.​ Failure to submit a proper notification may result in attendance points or \ndisciplinary action. \n \nResponsibilities \n \n●​ Employees must notify their immediate supervisor or the designated attendance \nreporting channel (Batphone, email, or any approved method). \n●​ Immediate supervisors/RTAs must log any reported attendance notifications into \nthe Zoho Attendance Notification Form if the employee fails to do so. \n \n \nHow to Submit Attendance Notification in Zoho \n \nEmployee Notification\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n●​ Employees must inform their immediate supervisor/RTA or use Batphone as \nsoon as they become aware that they will be late or absent. \n●​ Notifications must be made at least 2 hours before and 2 hours after that s/he will \nbe out of work. \n●​ If an employee fails to notify, it will be considered a No Call No Show (NCNS), \nwhich may lead to disciplinary action. \n \nStep 1: Access Zoho Attendance Notification Form \nAll notifications must be recorded in the Zoho Attendance Notification Form by \neither the employee or the immediate supervisor/RTA if the employee is unable to do \nso. \n \nA.​ Log in to Zoho Creator / Zoho Attendance Tool.​\n \nB.​ Select Attendance Notification Form.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \n \n●​ Required details to be filled out: \n \n○​ Employee Name \n○​ Channel of Notification (Batphone, Direct Message, Email, Supervisor \nReport, etc.) \n○​ Type of Notification (Absent or Late) \n○​ Reason for Absence or Tardiness (Personal, Medical, Emergency, etc.) \n○​ Expected Return Date (if applicable) \n○​ Additional Notes/Reasons (Supporting Documents, Expected Delays, etc.) \n \nAgent Responsibilities After Submission \n \n●​ Continue following instructions from TL or Operations. \n●​ Respond promptly to any follow-up or clarification requests. \n●​ Ensure future compliance with attendance policies. \n \nEscalation and Coordination \n \n●​ Escalate attendance issues to Operations (Immediate Support/TL/STL/OM) / \nWorkforce Management Team (WFM/RTA), if required. \n●​ Coordinate with RTA/WFM for plotting and documentation. \n \nCompliance and Monitoring\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n●​ Incomplete or late submissions may be tagged as unexcused. \n●​ All attendance records are subject to audit. \n●​ Repeated violations may result in disciplinary action.\n🎫 WFM / RTA Ticket\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n| WFM/RTA tickets Process \nPurpose/ Scope \nThe purpose of this SOP is to establish a standardized and organized process for \nrequesting, creating, and handling any RTA-related requests through WFM/RTA \ntickets. This includes, but is not limited to: \n● ​\nOffline activities (coaching, training, team huddles) \n● ​\nLunch movement requests \n● ​\nSchedule change requests \n● ​\nSchedule swaps \n● ​\nBidding-related requests \n● ​\nAny other workforce or real-time support requests managed by RTA \nThis SOP ensures proper documentation, accuracy, and cleanliness of ticket requests, \nallowing the RTA team to efficiently review, validate, and take action using Zoho. \nThis SOP applies to all support staff who are required to submit WFM/RTA-related \nrequests and to the RTA team responsible for monitoring and processing these \nrequests. \n \nRoles & Responsibilities \nList the key roles involved. \nRole                        ​​\nResponsibility \nSupport / TL  ​\n​\n• Submit accurate and timely ticket requests \n• Ensure complete details and supporting documents are \nprovided \n• Follow timelines stated in this SOP\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nRTA (Real-Time Analyst)   • Review and validate submitted tickets \n• Coordinate and update schedules accordingly \n• Resolve or escalate issues as needed \n \nTools / Requirements \nZoho Ticketing System \n \nProcedure (Steps) \nStep 1: Identify the Type of RTA Request \nSupport must first identify the nature of the request, such as: \n \n●​ Offline activity (coaching, training, team huddle) \n●​ Lunch movement \n●​ Schedule request or adjustment \n●​ Schedule swap \n●​ Bids-related request \n●​ Other RTA-related concerns \n \nStep 2: Ticket Request Timing ADD SCREENSHOTS \n \n●​ All RTA-related requests must be submitted at least one (1) hour before the \nintended effective time. \n●​ For planned activities (e.g., coaching, training, lunch movement), advance notice \nis required. \nExample: \n-​\nIf the request affects the schedule at 1:30 PM, the ticket must be \nsubmitted on or before 12:00 PM. \n \n Step 3: Create the Ticket in Zoho \nTo create a ticket, proceed to the RTA/WFM Ticketing System. When creating \nthe ticket, ensure the following details are clearly provided:\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \nType of RTA request (e.g., Lunch Movement, Schedule Swap, Coaching) \n●​ Date and exact time affected \n●​ Duration or impact timeframe \n●​ Reason or justification for the request \n●​ Name of requester and team \n●​ Any approvals required (if applicable) \n \nStep 4: Attach Supporting Documents (If Applicable) \n \nAttach screenshots or proof for requests or issues such as: \n●​ Internet connectivity problems \n●​ Zoho system or tool errors \n●​ Approved schedule changes or swaps \n \nStep 5: Submit and Monitor Ticket \n \n●​ Submit the ticket through Zoho. \n●​ Monitor the ticket status for updates or questions from RTA. \n●​ Respond promptly if additional clarification or documentation is requested. \n \nStep 6: RTA Review and Action  \n \n●​ RTA reviews the ticket for completeness and compliance with guidelines. \n●​ RTA approves, denies, or adjusts the request based on operational needs. \n●​ Any action taken is documented in the Zoho ticket.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nNotes / Tips \n●​\nIncomplete or late ticket submissions may result in delays or denial of the \nrequest. \n●​\nAlways double-check time and date accuracy before submitting. \n●​\nUse clear and professional language when describing the request. \n \nExceptions & Escalation \n●​ If issues occur (e.g., inability to submit a ticket, Zoho downtime, internet issues), \nsupport may directly contact any available RTA. \n●​ Escalation is allowed only when supporting documents (e.g., screenshots of \nerrors or connectivity issues) are provided. \n●​ Repeated non-compliance may be escalated to the Team Lead or Operation \nManager. \nQuality Check / Expected Result \nTo confirm the task was completed correctly: \n●​ The ticket was submitted within the required timeframe. \n●​ All required fields and details are complete and accurate. \n●​ Supporting documents are attached when applicable. \n●​ RTA acknowledgment or approval is recorded in Zoho. \nExpected Result: \n●​ Offline activity is properly documented and reflected in workforce \nscheduling or REST Tool\n🪵 Workforce Logs\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n| Workforce RTA Logs (Site-Wide, Account-Wide, Employee-Specific) \nPurpose / Scope \n●​ This SOP defines the standardized process for documenting, tracking, and escalating \noperational anomalies through the Workforce RTA Logs. It ensures visibility, \naccountability, and timely response to service-level risks, employee compliance issues, \nand technical disruptions. \n●​ This SOP applies to all Workforce RTAs responsible for real-time monitoring and \nintraday management across all sites and accounts. \n \nRoles & Responsibilities  \nRole \nResponsibility \nRTA \nIdentify issues, log incidents, attach evidence, and escalate \nwhen required. \nTeam Leader (TL) \nAct on employee-specific logs (coaching, NTE/NOD) \nSenior TL (STL) \nEnsure resolution and compliance \nOperations Manager \n(OM) \nAddress site-wide/account-wide risks \nIT / WFM \nResolve technical or system-related issues \n \nTools / Requirements \n●​ Zoho Creator – ECETrack Workforce RTA Logs \n●​ Company email \n●​ Monitoring tools (InContact,ServiceNow,Latte) \n●​ Supporting evidence (screenshots, AUX reports, chat logs)​\n \n \n \nTypes of RTA Logs \nEach entry in the RTA Logs must be categorized according to the scale of the impact:\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n1.​ Site-Wide​\n Used when the situation affects the entire site or a large population across multiple \naccounts.​\n Example: Regional power outage or building-level internet disruption.​\n \n2.​ Account-Wide​\n For issues specific to a program or client account.​\n Example: A tool outage affecting only the XYZ client account or SLA drops on ABC \nprogram.​\n \n3.​ Employee (Specific)​\n Used for incidents involving a specific team member.​\n Example: Agent caught sleeping or an internet issue at a home-based workstation.​\n \n \nCategories and Sub-Categories \nMain Category \nSub-Category \nDescription \nService Level & Volume \nManagement \nSLA Escalation – P1 \n(85%) \nSLA dips below 85% for more than 15 \nminutes. \nSLA Escalation – P0 \n(60%) \nSLA dips below 60% in any 15-minute \ninterval. \nHigh Abandonment \nRate \nABN rate exceeds threshold per \naccount standards. \nUnderstaffing Alert \nReal-time headcount drops below \nrequired levels. \nOverstaffing Alert \nHeadcount significantly exceeds \nintraday requirement. \nQueue Surge / Low \nQueue Alert \nSudden rise or drop in volume that’s not \nforecasted. \nAgent Behavior & \nCompliance \nPost Abandonment \nAgent logs out or disconnects while on \na live contact. \nSleeping \nAgent inactive and unresponsive during \nlive monitoring.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nUnauthorized Use of \nCellphone \nAgent caught using phone during shift. \nUnscheduled Break / \nIdle Time \nTaking breaks beyond allowed or no \nactive state for prolonged period. \nExtended \nNon-Productive AUX \nStaying in non-productive states too \nlong (e.g., Break, Meeting). \nAccessing \nNon-Working Related \nSites \nVisiting websites that are not related to \nyour job or work responsibilities during \nworking hours or while using company \nequipment or networks. \nPossible Protraction / \nWork Delay \nDelay caused by internal or external \nblockers. \nTechnical & \nInfrastructure Issues \nPower Outage \nComplete loss of electricity affecting \nagent(s). \nInternet Outage \nAgent unable to connect due to \nconnectivity issues. \nTools Outage \nSpecific systems or platforms are down \n(e.g., Salesforce, Zendesk). \nLatency Issues \nApplication lagging or slowing down \nproductivity. \nHeadset / Device \nFailure \nHardware problems (broken mouse, \nheadset, keyboard). \nProcess & Work \nDisruptions \nPossible Protraction / \nWork Delay \nDelay caused by internal or external \nblockers. \nWorkforce System \nDowntime \nZoho, Genesys, WFM tools become \ninaccessible or malfunction. \nSystem Maintenance \nImpact \nKnown/planned maintenance that \ninterrupts work hours. \n​\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \nProcedure (Steps)  \nStep 1: Identify the Situation \nMonitor intraday performance and agent behavior. \n​\n Proceed when: \n●​ SLA or ABN thresholds are breached  \n●​ Behavioral/compliance violations occur \n●​ Technical or infrastructure issues impact operations \nStep 2: Select the Log Type \nGo to this link:​Zoho Workforce RTA Logs​\n \nChoose the correct scope: \n●​ Site-Wide – Entire site or multiple accounts (Step-by-step filling guide) \n●​ Account-Wide – Specific program (Step-by-step filling guide) \n●​ Employee-Specific – Individual employee (Step-by-step filling guide) \nStep 3: Complete the Log Form \nFill in all required fields: \n●​ Date and Time of the Incident – When the issue occurred. \n●​ Site and/or Account Affected – Clearly indicate where the issue happened. \n●​ Type of Log – Confirm it is Site-Wide or Account-Wide. \n●​ Category / Sub-Category – Based on the nature of the incident. \n●​ Detailed Description – Briefly describe the situation, how it was discovered, what was \nobserved, and any relevant context. \n●​ Action Taken by RTA or Operations – Note any immediate steps, communication, \nescalation, or resolution attempts. \n●​ Status – Choose one:​\n \n○​ Resolved – if fully addressed \n○​ Ongoing – if still being monitored or partially resolved \n○​ Escalated – if forwarded to IT, Ops, or Management for action \nIMPORTANT NOTES: \n \n■​\nSite-Wide / Account-Wide: Status field is mandatory​\n \n■​\nEmployee-Specific: Recommendation field is required\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStep 4: Attach Evidence (if applicable) \nUpload: \n●​ Screenshots \n●​ System/AUX logs \n●​ Chat transcripts \nStep 5: Submit and Monitor \n●​ Submit the entry \n●​ Continue monitoring \n●​ Update the same log until fully resolved \nStep 6: Operations Action \nFor employee-specific logs: \n●​ TL/OM receives notification \n●​ Actions taken via:​\n \n○​ NTE/NOD button \n○​ Coaching button​\n \n●​ RTA validates completion (column updates to Yes) \nExceptions & Escalation \nIssue \nAction \nEscalate To \nSLA P0 / Tool outage \nImmediate logging & call-out \nOM / IT \nRepeated agent violations \nLog + evidence \nTL / STL \nNo action after 5 days \nFollow-up & document \nManager \nQuality Check / Expected Result \n●​ Correct log type selected \n●​ Complete and accurate details \n●​ Evidence attached when applicable \n●​ Status updated and closed properly \nRecords / Outputs \n●​ Workforce RTA Log entry \n●​ Email notifications\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n●​ NTE/NOD or Coaching records \nReferences \n●​ Workforce Logs SOP \n●​ Workforce RTA Logs SOP\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/\n🧒 Employee-Specific\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n|How to Log Workforce RTA Logs (Employee-Specific) \n \nStep 1: Access the Workforce RTA Log System \n●​ Open your preferred web browser. \n●​ Go to the designated Workforce RTA Log Form. \n \nStep 2: Select Type of Log \n●​ Choose \"Employee-Specific\" as the type of log entry.​\n \n \nStep 3: Identify the Employee \n●​ Select the Employee’s Name from the dropdown or input field.​\n \n●​ Select the Site and Account where the employee is assigned. \n \nStep 4: Choose the Appropriate Category and Sub-Category\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nUnder Agent Behavior & Compliance, select the relevant sub-category: \n●​ Post Abandonment – Agent disconnected/logged out during active contact.​\n \n●​ Sleeping – Agent inactive and unresponsive.​\n \n●​ Unauthorized Use of Cellphone – Agent caught using a phone while on duty.​\n \n●​ Unscheduled Break/Idle Time – Agent took excessive or unscheduled breaks.​\n \n●​ Extended Non-Productive AUX – Agent stayed too long in non-productive \nstates, including:​\n \n○​ Prolonged After Call Work (ACW) \n○​ Prolonged Average Handle Time (AHT) \n○​ Unauthorized usage of offline AUX \n○​ Logging out without approval \n○​ Any of the above that negatively affected the SLA \n \nStep 5: Fill in the Incident Details \nProvide the following information: \n●​ Date and Time of the Incident – When it happened. \n●​ Category/Sub-Category – Based on the agent’s behavior. \n●​ Detailed Description – Include what was observed or reported, how it was \nconfirmed (screenshots, chat logs, etc.), and any relevant patterns of behavior. \n \nStep 6: Upload Supporting Documents \n●​ Upload any evidence to support the log:​\n \n○​ Screenshots \n○​ Chat or system logs \n○​ AUX reports​\n \n●​ Recommendation: Attach an NTE/NOD recommendation or coaching \ndocumentation if applicable.​\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStep 7: Submit the Log Entry \n●​ Double-check all fields. \n●​ Click Submit or Save to log the report. \n \nStep 8: Monitoring and Operations Action \n●​ Once submitted, the Operations Team (TL, STL, Managers) will receive an \nautomated email notification about the RTA log.​\n \n●​ The Ops Team must respond by issuing an:​\n \n○​ NTE (Notice to Explain) or NOD (Notice of Disciplinary Action) \n○​ Logging a coaching session \nOnce submitted, the Operations Team (TL, STL, Managers) will receive an email \nalert with the report. \nWithin the email/system, they can: \nClick “NTE/NOD” to issue a disciplinary citation. \nClick “Coaching” to log a coaching form.​\n​\n \n \n​\n \nAccountability: \n❖​ The Immediate Supervisor (e.g., TL) is solely responsible for ensuring the \nincident is addressed. \n❖​ If the immediate supervisor is unavailable, responsibility follows the \nhierarchy (STL, then Manager). \n❖​ The Immediate Supervisor is expected to act within 5 calendar days from \nthe date the RTA log was submitted. \n❖​ Failure to act within 5 days will result in the Immediate Supervisor being \nheld accountable and cited for negligence.​\n \n●​ RTAs will monitor if the action has been completed and document the follow-up \non the same entry if needed.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/\n🏢 Site/Account Wide-Specific\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n|How to Log Workforce RTA Logs (Site-Wide / Account-Wide) \nRefer to this SOP from Programming Team: \n \nWorkforce Logs SOP\n \nProcedure \nStep 1: Access the Workforce RTA Log System \n●​ Open your preferred web browser. \n●​ Go to the designated Workforce RTA Log Form.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStep 2: Select the Log Type \n●​ Choose either:​\n \n○​ Site-Wide – if the issue affects an entire site or multiple accounts. \n○​ Account-Wide – if the issue is isolated to a specific account or program. \n \nStep 3: Identify the Affected Entity \n●​ For Site-Wide: Select the specific site name from the dropdown. \n●​ For Account-Wide: Select the account name or program affected. \n \nStep 4: Choose the Correct Category and Sub-Category \n●​ Use the predefined categories:​\n \n○​ Service Level & Volume Management \n○​ Agent Behavior & Compliance \n○​ Technical & Infrastructure Issues \n○​ Process & Work Disruptions​\n \n●​ Then select the appropriate sub-category that best describes the situation. \n \nStep 5: Provide Incident Details \nFill in the required fields with the following: \n●​ Date and Time of the Incident – When the issue occurred. \n●​ Site and/or Account Affected – Clearly indicate where the issue happened. \n●​ Type of Log – Confirm it is Site-Wide or Account-Wide. \n●​ Category / Sub-Category – Based on the nature of the incident. \n●​ Detailed Description – Briefly describe the situation, how it was discovered, \nwhat was observed, and any relevant context. \n●​ Action Taken by RTA or Operations – Note any immediate steps, \ncommunication, escalation, or resolution attempts. \n●​ Status – Choose one:​\n \n○​ Resolved – if fully addressed \n○​ Ongoing – if still being monitored or partially resolved \n○​ Escalated – if forwarded to IT, Ops, or Management for action\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \nStep 6: Submit and Monitor \n●​ Click Submit or Save once all fields are filled out. \n●​ Continue monitoring the situation even after logging. \n●​ If the issue persists or changes status, update the same log entry with the new \ndevelopments until fully resolved.​\n🚛 Employee Movement\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n|Employee Movement Processing \nPurpose / Scope \nThis SOP outlines how Workforce RTAs process employee movements such as \npromotions, demotions, account transfers, floating status, and leadership changes through Zoho \nHR Movement Forms. Applies to all Workforce RTAs handling movement requests from \nOperations. \n \nRoles & Responsibilities \nRole \nResponsibility \nOperations Team \nSubmit WFM ticket with complete details \nRTA \nValidate request and submit HR Movement Form \nWorkforce Manager \nValidate exceptions and urgent cases \nHR \nFinal processing and records update \n \nTools / Requirements \n●​ WFM Ticketing System \n●​ Zoho HR Movement Form \n●​ Supporting documents (approval emails, memos) \n \nProcedure (Steps) \nStep 1: Receive WFM Ticket \nOperations submits ticket with: \n●​ Employee name & ID \n●​ Movement type \n●​ Effective date \n●​ Supporting documents\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \nAll highlighted fields are required. \n \nStep 2: Validate Request \nRTA reviews tickets for accuracy. \n●​ If incomplete → return to Operations \n●​ If invalid → escalate to Workforce Manager/RTA Team Lead \n \nStep 3: Submit HR Movement Form  \nInput validated details into Zoho. Guided Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) for HR \nMovement Notification Form \n \nRemember:  \n○​\nThe account should always be Walmart. \n○​\nIf the employee belongs to another account, coordinate with the RTA of that account to \nensure a smooth transition. \n○​\nAlways coordinate with the Scheduler/Staffing POC.​\n \nSpecial Scenarios \n●​ Change of Account: Receiving program RTA processes \n●​ Floating/BENCH: Previous account RTA processes \n●​ Bulk Movements: Consolidated ticket required/Only for mass changes\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStep 4: Follow-Up & Closure \n●​ Monitor processing \n●​ Update WFM ticket \n●​ Close ticket once completed \n \nExceptions & Escalation \nIssue \nAction \nEscalate To \nIncomplete ticket \nRequest correction \nOperations \nUrgent movement \nPriority handling \nWorkforce Manager \nPayroll discrepancy Coordinate correction Discrepancy POC \n \nQuality Check / Expected Result \n●​ Correct movement reflected in system \n●​ Accurate effective date \n●​ Ticket properly closed \n \nRecords / Outputs \n●​ HR Movement Form \n●​ Updated employee records \n●​ Closed WFM ticket \n \nReferences \n●​ HR Movement SOP – Workforce RTA \n●​ Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) for HR Movement Notification Form_9/19/2023​\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \nFOR SUPPORT VIEW\n⭕ Resignation/Termination\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n|Resignation & Termination Processing \nPurpose / Scope \nThis SOP ensures accurate, compliant, and timely processing of employee \nresignations and terminations through Zoho, coordinating with HR and Operations. \nApplies to all Workforce RTAs. \n \nRoles & Responsibilities \nRole \nResponsibility \nOperations \nAcknowledge resignation / initiate termination \nRTA \nFile resignation/termination in Zoho \nHR \nFinal validation, exit processing \nEmployee \nSubmit formal resignation letter \n \nTools / Requirements \n●​ Zoho Resignation/Termination Form \n●​ Official resignation letter \n●​ APS records, ACHIEVE scores \n \nProcedure (Steps) \nStep 1: Notification \n●​ Employee submits resignation letter (Email) \n●​ Workforce RTA & HR must be CC’d \n●​ Verbal resignations are not accepted\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \nStep 2: Validate Details \nConfirm: \n●​ Last working day \n●​ Reason \n●​ Personal email & contact number \n●​ APS points & ACHIEVE scores \n●​ Rehire eligibility \n \nStep 3: File in Zoho \n●​ Access HR → Resignation/Termination Form \n●​ Complete all required fields \n●​ Submit for HR processing \n \nStep 4: Confirmation & Record Keeping \n●​ Send screenshot of submission to HR & Operations \n●​ Monitor approval status \n●​ Update BH Roster (Agent List, Daily team assignment and all agent active list \ntabs) \n●​ Reply to Email for confirmation \n \n \nExceptions & Escalation \nIssue \nAction \nEscalate To \nNo resignation letter \nDocument & proceed \nHR \nDisputed dates \nVerify before filing \nHR / Ops\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nAWOL cases \nProcess as termination \nHR \n \nQuality Check / Expected Result \n●​ Accurate resignation/termination date \n●​ Complete employee details \n●​ HR acknowledgment received \n \nRecords / Outputs \n●​ Zoho resignation/termination entry \n●​ Email confirmations \n●​ HR exit documentation \n \nReferences \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Workforce Real-Time Analyst (RTA)_020…\n✉️ Dispute\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n|Disputing \nStep-by-step Guide on how to file dispute \nPurpose \nThis SOP defines the proper handling, validation, and approval of employee disputes \nrelated to break taggings and log-in/log-out records. It ensures accurate \ntimekeeping, fair resolution, and compliance with scheduling and attendance policies. \nThis SOP applies to: \n●​ All employees submitting time-related disputes \n●​ RTAs acting as dispute approvers \n●​ Team Leads providing supporting confirmation when necessary \nAs an RTA, your role is to act as the approver and validator of disputes. Approval is \nnot automatic and must be based on strict verification. \nRTAs are responsible for ensuring that: \n●​ Submitted proofs are valid, clear, and timestamped \n●​ All dispute details are accurate and aligned with proof \n●​ Approved time adjustments correctly reflect the employee’s actual work time \n \nTypes of Disputes \nA. Break Disputes \nDefinition:​\nBreak disputes relate to specific taggings, such as: \n●​ Breaks \n●​ Meetings \n●​ Coachings \n●​ Other offline activities\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nPurpose:​\nTo confirm that the employee: \n●​ Returned on time from the activity \n●​ Properly resumed work \n●​ Was incorrectly tagged or affected by a system issue \nKey Objective:​\n​\n​\nEnsure that productivity and task tracking are accurate. \nB. Time Log Disputes \nDefinition:​\nDisputes filed when an employee’s actual log-in or log-out time was not properly \ncaptured by Zoho. \nPurpose:​\nTo correct: \n●​ Missing log-ins or log-outs \n●​ Errors caused by tool or connectivity issues \n \nDispute Filing Requirements \nAll disputes must include timestamped proof showing that the employee: \n●​ Was present and working \n●​ Returned from break or activity on time \n●​ Logged in or logged out as scheduled \n●​ Filed within 5 Days \nDisputes without proof should not be approved. \nA. Hierarchy of Acceptable Proofs \nRTAs must evaluate proof using the following priority order: \n1.​ IC (In-Contact) Stamps \n○​ Highest and most reliable proof\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n2.​ Messages Showing Availability or Return \n○​ Chat messages confirming the employee is back \ni.​ Issue Tracker \n○​ Must include visible timestamps \n3.​ Screenshot of Issue Encountered \n○​ Login errors, tool issues, system downtime \n○​ Date and time must be visible \n4.​ Team Lead Vouch \n○​ Confirmation from the employee’s Team Lead \n○​ Used only if higher-priority proofs are unavailable \nB. RTA Validation Checklist (Mandatory) \nBefore approving any dispute, the RTA must verify all of the following: \n✅ Date matches the disputed shift date \n✅ Scheduled start and end of shift are correct \n✅ Working hours per day are accurate \n✅ Log status (Whole Day, Half Day, etc.) is appropriate \n✅ Time In and Time Out exactly match the proof provided \n✅ Reason selected aligns with the proof and explanation \n✅Filed within 5 days of disputed date \n⚠️ Time In or Time Out must NOT be adjusted unless it exactly matches the \ntimestamp shown in the proof. \nC. Approval Guidelines \nA dispute may be approved only if: \n●​ Proof is valid and follows the proof hierarchy \n●​ All form fields are accurate and consistent \n●​ Time adjustments are justified by the evidence \nA dispute should be rejected or returned if:\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n●​ Proof is missing, unclear, or inconsistent \n●​ Timestamps do not match the requested adjustment \n●​ Details (schedule, hours, log status) are incorrect, unless adjustable. \n●​ Filed more than 5 days after. (Redirect employee to Lemuel Ching) \nRTAs should add notes when clarification or justification is required. \nD. Documentation and Accountability \n●​ Approved disputes must include: \n○​ Correct reason selection \n○​ Admin or RTA notes if applicable \n●​ Dispute records must be maintained for audit and tracking \n●​ Repeated disputes from the same employee may be escalated \n \nImportant Reminders \n●​ RTAs act as gatekeepers, not endorsers \n●​ Proof quality outweighs explanations \n●​ IC stamps take precedence over all other proofs \n●​ Team Lead vouch is a last-resort validation, not a default \n●​ Accuracy is critical—approved disputes directly affect payroll and reporting\nError Checking\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n|Error Checking on Zoho \nPurpose \nTo ensure that all Zoho time log records accurately reflect employee \nattendance, work hours, and leave status. Error checking allows RTAs to identify \ndiscrepancies caused by system issues, missing data, or incorrect tagging, and to take \nthe necessary corrective actions.  \n \nWhat Is Error Checking \nError checking is a validation process where RTAs review Zoho records to confirm that: \n●​ Login and logout times are accurate \n●​ Working Hours Per Day (WHPD) are properly recorded \n●​ Leave, OT, and absence tagging are correct \n●​ Weekly and daily work hours are computed correctly \nIf discrepancies are found, RTAs initiate the appropriate correction or escalation. \n \n \nKey Principles of Error Codes \nA key principle of Error Checking is that an Error Code does not automatically \nconfirm an error. The code only flags a potential discrepancy. The RTA\'s mandatory \nrole is to manually review the log entry associated with the code to validate the data \nand confirm if a correction is genuinely needed. RTAs must check every log that the \ncode pertains to, regardless of initial error presence. \n \nHow Error Codes Work \n●​ The Error Checking column in Zoho displays a number \n●​ Each number corresponds to a specific attendance or logging issue\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \nError Code Reference and Explanation \n0 – No Error \n●​ Record is correct \n●​ No action required \n1 – Absent (No Login) \n●​ Note column = Absent (No Login) \n●​ Login column is empty \n●​ Absent column = 0 \nAction:​\nValidate if the employee was truly absent or if there is a missing login record. \n2 – Missing Logout \n●​ Login column is not empty \n●​ Logout column is empty \nAction:​\nVerify logout proof and update logout time if valid. \n3 – Missing Schedule and WHPD \n●​ Start Schedule = 0 \n●​ End Schedule = 0 \n●​ WHPD = 0 \n●​ Login column is not empty \nAction:​\nLikely a scheduling or system issue. Validate schedule and correct WHPD. \n4 – Approved Full-Day Leave \n●​ With approved full-day leave \n●​ Login column is empty \n●​ Absent column > 0\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nAction:​\nNo correction needed if leave is valid. \n5 – Short Login Duration \n●​ Login column is not empty \n●​ Login hours < 1 hour \nAction:​\nCheck if this is a partial log, system issue, or incorrect tagging. \n6 – Incorrect Status with Absence \n●​ Status is not Half Day (1st or 2nd) \n●​ Login column is not empty \n●​ Absent column > 0 \nAction:​\nValidate whether status should be Half Day or corrected absence. \n7 – Agent-Specific Rule \n●​ Applies only to Jenife Tubac Garcia \nAction:​\nFollow special handling rules provided for this agent. \n8 – Insufficient Login Hours (Whole Day / Training / Pre-Shift OT) \n●​ Status = Whole Day OR Whole Day – Training OR Pre-Shift OT \n●​ Login hours < required minimum \nMinimum Login Requirement: \n●​ WHPD = 8 → Login ≥ 6 hours \n●​ WHPD = 10 → Login ≥ 7 hours \nAction:​\nValidate logs and adjust status or hours if needed. \n9 – Half Day with Missing Logout\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n●​ Status = Half Day (1st or 2nd) \n●​ Login column is not empty \n●​ Logout column is empty \n●​ No HD leave filed \nAction:​\nVerify logout proof or update status accordingly. \n10 – Missing Login with WHPD \n●​ Login column is empty \n●​ WHPD > 0 \n●​ No approved full-day leave \n●​ Absent column = 0 \nAction:​\nConfirm if this is a system error or true no-login case. \n10 - WHPD vs. Sick Leave Reconciliation \n●​ When SL ≠ WHPD → \"Over-filed\" or under-filed. \n●​ SL and WHPD do not match (e.g., SL 10 hrs for 8-hr shift). \nAction:​\nDeny/Return SL request if incorrect and/or Manually adjust SL or WHPD if urgent \nand authorized. \n11 – Missing Login with Absence \n●​ Login column is empty \n●​ WHPD > 0 \n●​ No approved full-day leave \n●​ Absent column ≠ WHPD \nAction:​\nCheck if absence should match WHPD or if correction is needed. \n12 – Missing Login and Notes \n●​ Login column is empty \n●​ WHPD > 0\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n●​ No approved full-day leave \n●​ Absent column = 0 \n●​ Note column is empty \nAction:​\nRequire clarification or proof before correction. \n13 – Missing Status and Login \n●​ No approved full-day leave \n●​ Status column is not null \n●​ Login column is null \n●​ HD Leave ≠ 2 \nAction:​\nValidate leave or login details and correct record. \n14 – Approved VTO \n●​ With approved full-day leave \n●​ Leave type = VTO \nAction:​\nNo correction needed if approval is valid. \n15 – MedLOA Case \n●​ Login column is not empty \n●​ Leave type = MedLOA \nAction:​\nEscalate or validate according to MedLOA policy. \n16 – Absent with Late or Undertime \n●​ Absent = WHPD \n●​ Late or Undertime > 0 \n●​ Login column is empty \n●​ Note contains “ABSENT”\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nAction:​\nValidate if tagging is correct or requires adjustment. \n17 – Absence with Supporting Issues \n●​ Absent > 0 \n●​ WHPD > 0 \n●​ Clinic OR Lost Power OR Lost Internet > 0 \nAction:​\nValidate proof and ensure proper dispute handling. \n18 – Half Day Login Hour Validation \n●​ Status = HD (1st or 2nd) \n●​ Approved HD leave \n●​ Login hours = Half WHPD + 2 hours \nMinimum Login Requirement: \n●​ WHPD = 8 → Login ≥ 6 hours \n●​ WHPD = 10 → Login ≥ 7 hours \nAction:​\nFlag if login hours are below the required threshold. \n19 – Conflicting Status with Login \n●​ Note column = Absent (No Login) \n●​ Login and Logout columns are not empty \n●​ Status = Pre-Shift OT OR Whole Day OR Whole Day – Training \nAction:​\nCorrect note or status to align with actual login activity. \n20 – Break Logs on Day Off \n●​ Break logs exist \n●​ Note contains “DAY OFF” \n●​ Login column is empty\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nAction:​\nValidate if this is an incorrect break tag or scheduling error.\nAPS Scrubbings\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n|APS Scrubbing SOP \nPurpose/Scope \nThis SOP outlines the step-by-step process for APS (Attendance Pointing System) \nScrubbing using Zoho, ensuring accurate attendance records, proper point application, \nand compliance with company policies.This process applies to all team leads, \nworkforce, or designated personnel responsible for reviewing, validating, and correcting \nattendance records in Zoho. \n \nRoles and Responsibilities \nAgent – Ensures proper logging in/out and files necessary attendance-related requests. \nTeam Lead – Conducts initial review and validation of attendance records. \nWorkforce – Performs final validation and approves corrections when required. \n \nAPS Scrubbing Step-by-Step Process \nStep 1: Access Zoho \n●​ Log in to Zoho \n●​ Navigate to APS Reports \n●​ Click APS Report (Admin) \nStep 1.1 \n○​ For easy monitoring, View Zoho Timelogs Checker Dashboard. \n○​ Refresh data. \n○​ Promptly modify the date range for dates desired. \nStep 2: Select the Scrubbing Period \n●​ Identify the date to be scrubbed. \n●​ Filter attendance records by:\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n​\n * Date (Date range; From start date to yesterday’s date) \n​\n * Account (“walmart”) \n​\n * New APS is greater than 0 \n \nComprehensive guide of APS Guidelines, please refer to ECE Memorandum \nStandardized Attendance Pointing System 2023 \nStep 3: Review Attendance Records \n​\na. Check each employee’s record for the following: \n●​ Missing login or logout \n●​ Late login or early logout \n●​ Absence or no log-in detected \n●​ NCNS \n●​ Incomplete or incorrect punches \n​\nb. Cross-check records with: \n●​ Approved leave requests \n●​ Filed tickets and/or approved VL/SL and approved disputes  (VL, \nSL, OT, coaching, meeting, clinic, etc.) \n​\nNote: Suspension will not accrue APS points. (As per Infraction of \nCompany Rules - Attendance Pointing System 2023 | Guidelines) \nStep 4: Validate Supporting Documentation \n​\na. Confirm if the employee has submitted: \n●​ Attendance correction request \n●​ Approved leave request \n●​ Meeting, coaching, or clinic ticket \n​\nb. Ensure all documents are:\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n●​ Properly approved \n●​ Filed within the timely filing period \nStep 5: Apply or Remove APS Points \n​\na. Based on validation, determine if APS points should be: \n​\n​\n* Applied (no valid justification or missing documentation) \n​\n​\n* Removed or Adjusted(valid and approved documentation present) \n​\nb. Update the APS points in Zoho accordingly. \nStep 6: Update Attendance Status in Zoho \n​\na. Correct the attendance status/time logs (e.g., Present, Absent, Leave, NCNS, \nLate) \n​\nb. Add clear and detailed remarks (e.g., Reason for adjustment) \nStep 7: Final Review and Save \n​\na. Double-check all updates for accuracy. \n​\nb. Save changes in Zoho. \n​\nc. Ensure the record reflects the correct APS points and attendance status. \n \nQuality Check and Compliance \n●​ APS scrubbing must be documented in Zoho. \n●​ No changes should be made without valid proof and approval. \n●​ Ensure consistency with company attendance and disciplinary policies.\n📗 Break Logs (HD, UT, LATE, Lost \nPower/Internet)\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n|Break Logs \nPurpose / Scope \nThis SOP defines the standardized process for logging break auxiliaries (Auxes) \nin Zoho related to power outages, internet loss, and system issues. It ensures \naccurate timekeeping, payroll correctness, and consistent handling of incidents for both \noffice-based and work-from-home (WFH) employees. \nZoho has 3 available break auxes for situations where there are Power outages, \ninternet outage or system issue. \n \n \n \nSystem Error : Tool issue within the PC unit (client or ECE regardless). Non deductible. \nLost Power : Power / Electricity outage causing non-productive hours. \nLost Internet : Internet connectivity outage causing non-productive hours. \n \nOffice Based Employees \n \nFor all office based employees with any issues with regards to power outage or internet \noutage, we’ll automatically add a break log for the respective outage. Take note that \nnone of these logs will be deductible from the employees payroll so MAKE SURE TO \nTICK the Not Payroll Deductible Checkbox.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nWork From Home Based Employees \n \nFor all work from home employees with any issues with regards to power outage or \ninternet outage, we’ll follow the flowchart outlined below: \n \n \nOutages TL;DR: \n \n●​ If the outage cannot be resolved within an hour, have the agent report to the \noffice. \n●​ If an agent can report, then add outage logs from the time the issue started to the \ntime the agent got to the office. Make sure to not tick the NOT PAYROLL \nDEDUCTIBLE box as this should be docked from their pay. \n●​ If the agent cannot report to the office, then logout agent and add outage logs \nfrom start of issue to end of shift. Make sure to not tick the NOT PAYROLL \nDEDUCTIBLE box as this should be docked from their pay. \n●​ If outage is resolved within an hour, add outage logs from start of issue to end of \nissue. \n \nIssue TL;DR:\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \n●​ If issue is resolvable by the IT, then add issue logs from start of issue to end of \nissue \n●​ If the issue is not resolvable, have the agent report to the office. \n●​ If an agent can report, then add system issue logs from the time the issue started \nto the time agent got to the office. \n●​ If the agent cannot report to the office, then logout agent and add system issue \nlogs from start of issue to end of shift. \n \nReference \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Workforce Real-Time Analyst (RTA)_020…\n📒 Suspension\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n|Suspension \nAll employee suspensions must be properly documented and plotted by the \nWorkforce Real-Time Adherence (RTA) team to ensure: \n●​ Accurate staffing projections \n●​ Prevention of unauthorized system access \n●​ Prevention of leave filings during suspension periods​\n \nSuspensions may occur due to: \n●​ Attendance Pointing System (APS) violations \n●​ Other employee handbook violations \n●​ Preventive suspensions \nSuspension Due to Handbook Violations & Preventive Suspension \n1. Suspension Due to Handbook Violations and Preventive Suspension \n1.​ Operations Team Request: \n○​ The Operations team must file a Workforce Management (WFM) ticket \nselecting the category “Suspension Request” and indicating: \n■​ Employee name and details \n■​ Violation or reason for suspension \n■​ Recommended suspension dates \n■​ Any relevant documentation (e.g., NOD, screenshots, or case \nnotes)\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n2.​ Coordination with RTA: \n○​ The Operations team must coordinate with the assigned RTA for the \nprogram. \n○​ The RTA will evaluate the proposed suspension dates based on staffing \navailability. \n○​ Adjustments may be recommended to minimize staffing impact while \nensuring compliance with disciplinary action timelines. \n3.​ Filing the Suspension in Zoho: \n○​ The RTA will input the approved suspension details into the Zoho Leave \nRequest (Suspension) Form (NOT the standard Leave Request Form). \n○​ The suspension must be properly labeled with the reason and approved \ndates. \n○​ The RTA must confirm the final plotted suspension with the Operations \nteam. \n​\n​\n​\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n4.​ Preventing Unauthorized Work During Suspension: \n○​ Once filed, the suspension details must be logged to prevent the affected \nemployee from: \n■​ Logging into the system on the suspension date \n■​ Filing Sick Leave (SL) or Vacation Leave (VL) during the \nsuspension period \n○​ If the employee attempts to log in or file leave, the RTA must notify the \nOperations team immediately for corrective action. \n \n2. Suspension Due to Attendance Pointing System (APS) \n1.​ Receipt of NOD for Suspension:​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n \n○​ The APS Point of Contact (POC) creates the Notice of Decision (NOD) \nfor Suspension for an employee due to APS violations. \n○​ The APS POC must coordinate with the assigned RTA and Operations \nteam to determine the appropriate suspension date. \n2.​ Scheduling Suspension Dates:​​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n \n○​ The RTA will evaluate the staffing impact and work with the Operations \nteam to select the best dates for suspension. \n○​ Adjustments can be made to avoid staffing shortages while ensuring \ncompliance with the APS disciplinary process. \n3.​ Filing in Zoho:​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n \n○​ Once a date is confirmed, the APS POC must log the suspension in the \nZoho Leave Request (Suspension) Form, ensuring all required details \nare included. \n○​ The reason for suspension must be clearly labeled as APS Suspension \nto differentiate it from other disciplinary suspensions. \n4.​ Ensuring Compliance:​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n \n○​ The RTA must cross-check employee schedules to ensure no conflicting \nleave requests exist. \n○​ If an employee attempts to file leave or log in on their suspension date, the \nRTA must escalate the issue to the Operations team for intervention.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \n3. Situational Events and Mitigation Plans \nScenario 1: Employee Attempts to Work on a Suspension Date \nIssue: Employee logs in despite suspension. \nMitigation: \n●​ RTA flags the login activity immediately. \n●​ Notify Operations team. \n●​ If intentional → Escalate to HR for further disciplinary action. \n●​ If system-related → Engage IT/Programming to correct access controls. \n \nScenario 2: Employee Files Leave on a Suspension Date \nIssue: Employee files SL/VL to avoid suspension. \nMitigation: \n●​ RTA rejects any leave request overlapping the suspension. \n●​ Operations reminds employee:​\n \n○​ Suspension days are mandatory \n○​ Suspension days cannot be converted to leave days. \n \nScenario 3: Suspension Conflicts with Critical Staffing Needs \nIssue: Suspension coincides with high call volume or peak period. \nMitigation: \n●​ RTA recommends alternate dates with lower demand. \n●​ If adjustment is not possible: \n○​ Implement temporary staffing or coverage measures.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nScenario 4: Operations Fails to Submit Suspension Request \nIssue: Violation confirmed, but no WFM ticket submitted. \nMitigation: \n●​ RTA proactively follows up with Operations. \n●​ If delay is critical: \n○​ Escalate to the Workforce Manager or HR Director to ensure compliance. \n \n4. Final Confirmation and Documentation \n●​ RTA confirms final suspension dates with Operations once plotted. \n●​ All suspension records must be retained for audit purposes. \n●​ HR must be informed of any discrepancies or violations of process. \n \n \n5. Reference \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Workforce Real-Time Analyst (RTA)_020…\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/\n🏷️ WF REST Attendance Aux Tagging\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n|WF REST Request and Process \n \nPurpose / Scope \nTo standardize the request process for offline activities (Coaching, Meetings, Training) \nand schedule adjustments. This process ensures the RTA has sufficient lead time to \nbalance floor coverage and that no agent \"misses\" a break due to a leadership request. \n \n \nThe \"1-Hour Rule\" Policy \n●​ Standard Requests: All tickets must be submitted a minimum of 1-hour prior to \nthe requested start time. \n●​ Late Requests: Any ticket submitted less than 1 hours in advance is subject to \ndenial if the capacity indicator is not in the \"Green\" zone on Workforce Rest, \nmeaning the volume vs capacity is critical during the requested timeframe.  \n \n \nProcedure: Creating & Submitting Tickets  \nStep 1: Impact Assessment  \nBefore submitting a ticket, the TL must check the agent’s current schedule in \nWorkforce Rest. \n●​ Identify Overlaps: Check if the requested offline time (e.g., Coaching from 2:00 \nPM – 3:00 PM) overlaps with the agent’s pre-plotted Break or Lunch. \n●​ Proactive Planning: If an overlap exists, the TL must decide on a proposed \nnew time for that break/lunch before sending the ticket. \nStep 2: Ticket Creation Requirements  \nWhen filing the ticket, the following information is mandatory for approval: \n1.​ Activity Type: (e.g., Coaching,Team Huddle, Meeting). \n2.​ Duration: Specific Start and End times. \n3.​ Schedule Adjustment Note: If the activity covers a pre-plotted break, the TL \nmust include \n○​ “This activity covers the 2:15 PM Break. Requesting to move this break to \n3:00 PM.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nNote: Movement of break is still subject to approval and is still not \nguaranteed that requested break schedule will be granted.  \nExample Given:  \n \nTemplate:  \nActivity: \nTime: From - To \n​\nDuration: \n​\nNote: Optional \n \nStep 3: Submission & RTA Sync \n●​ Submit: Send the ticket through the official ticketing portal. \n●​ Notify: Send a quick \"heads up\" to the RTA via Zoho Cliq with the ticket number. \n●​ Confirmation: The activity is not approved until the RTA moves the ticket to \"In \nProgress\" or \"Approved.\" Do not pull the agent off until this status change occurs. \n \nHandling Tool Maintenance (Contingency) \nIf Workforce Rest is under maintenance, the ticketing process remains the \nsame, but the validation changes: \n●​ TL Action: Submit the ticket as usual. \n●​ Validation: The RTA will manually check the IC (Interactive Center) and the \nBreak Schedule Sheet. \n●​ Expectation: If approved, the RTA will keep the ticket \"In Progress\" with a note: \n\"Approved manually; will be plotted once tool is online.\"  \n●​ Agent Movement: Once the RTA gives the \"Go\" via Zoho Cliq/Ticket note, the \nTL may proceed with the activity.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \n5. Expected Results & Effectiveness \nRequirement \nResult of Compliance \n1-Hour Lead Time \nAllows RTA to \"Level Load\" the floor, preventing sudden drops \nin service levels. \nBreak Movement \nLogic \nEnsures agent well-being and labor law compliance by \nguaranteeing no break is \"lost\" to a coaching session. \nClear Ticket Notes Reduces back-and-forth communication, speeding up the \napproval process. \nAudit Readiness \nCreates a clear history of why schedules were changed, \nprotecting the TL during performance reviews. \n \n \nEscalation Matrix \n●​ Urgent/Same-Day Needs: If a \"Critical Coaching/Meeting\" is needed in less than \n1 hour, an approval from STL/OM shall be required on the ticketing process for \napproval from the RTA’s.  \n●​ Missed Breaks: If a TL fails to include the break movement in the ticket and the \nagent misses their slot, the TL is responsible for the resulting adherence hit.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/\n📋 Meeting/Coaching/Clinic Ticketing \nFor Rest\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n|Meeting/Coaching/Clinic Ticketing For Rest \nPurpose \nTo establish a standardized process for filing and processing rest adjustment tickets in \nZoho when an employee attends a meeting, coaching, or clinic that overlaps with their \nscheduled rest period. \n \nScope \nThis SOP applies to all employees required to attend official meetings, coaching \nsessions, or clinics during their scheduled rest/break time and to the Support and \nWorkforce team responsible for validation and approval. \n \nResponsibility \nTeam Leaders: File rest tickets accurately and within the prescribed timeframe. \nWorkforce: Review, approve, and apply adjustments in REST \nDefinitions \n●​ Rest Ticket: A Zoho ticket filed to request adjustment or replacement of a \nrest period affected by work-related activities. \n \nProcedure  \nStep 1. Schedule Validation  \n●​ Confirm the date and time of the meeting, coaching, or clinic visit. \n●​ Verify that the session overlaps or replaces the scheduled rest period based on \nthe agent’s shift schedule. \nStep 2. Eligibility Check\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nA rest ticket may be filed if: \n●​ The activity is official and work-related. \n●​ The activity interrupts or consumes the employee’s scheduled rest time. \nStep 3. Access Zoho Ticketing & Ticket Creation \n●​ Log in to Zoho \n●​ Navigate and click RTA/WFM Ticketing \n●​ Select the appropriate Category ( Meeting/Coaching/Clinic ) \n●​ Select the Issue Type / Reason ( Rest Adjustment/ Rest Ticket ) \n●​ Fill out description box with necessary information (Date & Time in EST, Name of \nAgents, Detailed information) \n●​ Upload Documents (if needed) \n●​ Click submit \nStep 4.  Ticket Details Entry \n●​ Complete all required fields accurately \n●​ Type of Activity: Meeting / Coaching / Clinic \n●​ Date of Activity (EST) \n●​ Actual Start and End Time (EST) \n●​ Affected Rest Period \n●​ Detailed Description \nStep 5. Supporting Documentation  \nAttach applicable proof, if required: \n- Calendar invitation \n- Coaching or clinic schedule \n- Official meeting notice or endorsement \nStep 6.  Ticket Submission  \n●​ Review all information for accuracy and completeness. \n●​ Click Submit. \n●​ Record the Zoho ticket reference number or ID number for tracking. \n●​\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStep 7. Review and Approval  \nWorkforce review the ticket for: \n​\n- Validity of activity \n​\n- Accuracy of time and rest impact \n​\n- Completeness of documentation \n​\n- Approved tickets are processed for adjustments in REST \nStep 8. Rest Adjustment Implementation  \n●​ Once approved, the adjusted period is reflected in REST. \n●​ The employee must ensure: \n​\n- Proper IC tagging \n​\n- No overlapping or incorrect entries \n \nTurnaround Time \n●​ Rest tickets must be filed within the prescribed filing period (e.g., 30 \nminutes or 1 hour before the requested meeting or coaching). \n●​ Late submissions may result in non-approval. \n \nCompliance \nFailure to follow this SOP may lead to: \n●​ Disapproval of rest adjustments \n●​ Attendance discrepancies \n●​ Possible attendance points or corrective action\n📋 Workforce Rest Filing\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n|WFM REST Tool Management \nPurpose / Scope \nThe purpose of this procedure is to standardize how Real-Time Analysts (RTAs) \nmanage agent schedules, optimize breaks, and track offline activities using Workforce \nRest. This ensures optimal floor coverage, accurate shrinkage reporting, and data \nintegrity by accounting for every agent’s status in real-time. This SOP applies to all \nRTAs and covers daily operations from shift start to end-of-day (EOD) scrubbing. \n \nRoles & Responsibilities \n●​ Role: Real-Time Analyst (RTA) \n○​ Responsibility: Monitor capacity indicators, optimize breaks, tag \nabsences (NCNS/VL/SL/LOA), plot offline activities (Coaching/Meetings), \nand scrub logs for data accuracy. \n●​ Role: Team Lead (TL) / Operations Manager \n○​ Responsibility: Request offline activities via the RTA ticketing system, \nprovide clarification on agent attendance discrepancies, and ensure \nagents adhere to the schedules plotted. \n \nTools / Requirements \n●​ Workforce Rest: Primary tool for real-time tracking and break optimization. \n●​ Zoho Leave Requests: Used to verify approved Vacation Leave (VL) and Sick \nLeave (SL). \n●​ Communication Tool - Zoho Cliq : For coordination with Operations.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nProcedure (Steps) \nStep 1: Shift Start Break Audit & Optimization  \nImmediately at the start of the shift, the RTA must identify and assign breaks to agents \nmissing them. \n●​ Click the \"No Break\" button to filter for agents with empty break schedules.​\n \n●​ Tick the checkboxes for all agents in the filtered list. \n●​ Click the \"Optimize Breaks\" button (top right of the control dashboard)​\n \n●​ Result: The system automatically assigns breaks based on staffing needs to \nkeep the capacity indicator Green. \nStep 2: Mandatory Absence Tagging \nAccount for all agents not present on the floor within the first 30–60 minutes of the shift. \n●​ Tag missing agents as Absent if the associate is confirmed that there is no \nactivity during the expected shift. Indication is marked on Workforce Rest \nwhether the associate has logged in Zoho or has no logs during the shift.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n​\n \n●​ If Validated that agent is absent within the day. Mark the associate as absent in \nthe tool by simply right clicking Edit Schedule then click the 2nd bar under the \nagent name.​\n \n●​ Open Zoho Attendance/Leave: Run a report or filter the calendar for the current \nshift date. \n●​ Identify Leaves: List all agents marked for Vacation Leave (VL), Sick Leave \n(SL), or Leave of Absence (LOA), etc.  \n●​ Mark the associates that are out of office as absent in Workforce Rest.  \nStep 3: Break Ticketing System \nMonitor and review ticketing requests from operations regarding break and lunch \nmovements.  \n●​ Upon receiving a ticket from the ticketing system, review the break movement \nrequest from operations. Validation is required using IC tool and/or Workforce \nRest to identify if our shrinkage is manageable on the requested timeframe of the \nticket.  \n●​ Once valid, RTA must plot the break schedule requested on the tool for \ndocumentation and real time monitoring on their break time.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n●​ Monitoring adherence on all break schedules is mandatory for reporting. \nEmployees failing to comply with punctuality on his/her adherence to break \nschedule shall be subject to corrective action. \nStep 4: Schedule Scrubbing & Aux Adherence Enforcement \nThe RTA is responsible for performing a daily scrub to identify agents who did not \nadhere to their scheduled Aux tagging. \n1.​ Daily Scrubbing: RTAs will go through the logs which could be found on the \nupper left part of the system (stats), this is to identify agents who used incorrect \nAux codes or failed to follow the plotted schedule (Out of Adherence).​\n \n2.​ First & Second Violations: Recorded for tracking and reporting in the daily \nadherence dump file.  \n3.​ Third Violation: If an agent fails to adhere to their schedule for the 3rd time, the \nRTA shall officially send a Workforce Log for Coaching to the agent and their \nrespective Team Lead. \n4.​ Fourth Violation: If an agent is found out of adherence for the 4th time, an NTE \n(Notice to Explain) shall be issued for the agent to initiate the formal disciplinary \nprocess. \n \nContingency Procedure: Tool Downtime & Maintenance \nIn the event that Workforce Rest is offline or undergoing maintenance, the RTA must \ntransition to manual validation to ensure service continuity.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStep 1: Manual Validation of Requests When a ticket is received for a Break \nMovement during downtime: \n●​ Check IC (Incontact Tool): Verify the agent\'s current live status and the current \ncall queue/interval volume. \n●​ Consult Break Schedule Sheet: Refer to the sheet to see if the requested \nmovement conflicts with existing coverage requirements, checking on the break \nand lunch scheduled for the requested time ensures that we have our staffing \ncapacity under control and manage our shrinkage appropriately.  \nStep 2: Ticket Management & Approval If the request is deemed Valid based on \nmanual volume checks: \n●​ Update Ticket Status: Set the ticket to \"In Progress\". \n●​ Mandatory Internal Note: Add a note to the ticket using the following template:​\n\"Workforce Rest is currently under maintenance. Request has been manually \nvalidated and is APPROVED. Activity will be plotted in the tool for data integrity \nonce the system is back online.\" \n●​ Communication: Notify the requesting Team Lead via Zoho Cliq that they may \nproceed with the movement based on the manual approval. \nStep 3: Post-Maintenance Reconciliation Once Workforce Rest is back online: \n●​ The RTA must immediately plot all \"In Progress\" requests from the downtime \nperiod. \n●​ Close the tickets once the data is reflected in the tool to ensure shrinkage \nreporting remains accurate. \n \nEffectiveness of Procedure \n●​ Zero Operational Delay: Prevents \"bottlenecks\" where TLs feel they cannot \nmove agents because the tool is down. \n●​ Audit Trail Maintenance: By keeping tickets \"In Progress\" with specific notes, \nthere is a clear paper trail for WFM Managers to see why adherence might look \n\"off\" during maintenance windows. \n●​ Data Recovery: Ensures that even if the tool is down, the intent to track data \nremains, leading to 100% data capture once the system is restored.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nExpected Results & Effectiveness Indicators \nThe effectiveness of this SOP is measured by the stability of the floor and the accuracy \nof the data. Successful execution of these steps should result in: \n●​ Optimized Service Levels: By using the \"Optimize Breaks\" function, the \ncapacity indicator remains Green, ensuring we have the right number of people \nto handle incoming volume. \n●​ Reduced Unaccounted Shrinkage: Mandatory tagging within the first 60 \nminutes ensures that agents that are absent are removed from capacity math \nimmediately. \n●​ Data Integrity: Daily scrubbing ensures that payroll and performance reports \n(derived from Zoho and Workforce Rest) match 100%, reducing manual \ncorrections at the end of the month. \n●​ Improved Adherence: The 3rd and 4th violation triggers (Coaching and NTE) \nhold agents accountable to the optimized schedule and reduce Aux misuse.\n📞 Line Assignment\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nClient Tool Management \n \nPurpose \nTo define the proper use and management of client tools required for daily operations, \nmonitoring, and workload assignment, ensuring uninterrupted access, accurate tracking, and \ncompliance with client requirements. \n \nClient Tools Overview \nThere are three (3) primary client tools used in operations: \n1.​ VDI (Virtual Desktop Infrastructure) \n2.​ InContact (IC) \n3.​ ServiceNow (SNow) \n \nTool Descriptions and Usage \n1. VDI (Virtual Desktop Infrastructure) \n●​ VDI serves as the primary access point to all client tools \n●​ Both InContact (IC) and ServiceNow (SNow) can only be accessed through VDI \n●​ VDI functions as the Walmart virtual desktop environment \nWithout VDI access, agents and RTAs cannot use IC or SNow. \n \n2. InContact (IC) Add screenshot \n●​ IC is used to monitor agent tagging and activity status \n●​ Tracks: \n○​ Productive work\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n○​ Offline activities (breaks, meetings, coaching, etc.) \n○​ Time in and time out for the client side \n●​ IC functions similarly to Zoho, but serves as the client’s official time tracking tool \nSupervisory Capabilities: \n●​ RTAs can supervise agents in IC \n●​ Agents may be forcefully logged out if system issues or events prevent them from \nlogging out properly \n \n3. ServiceNow (SNW) Add screenshot \n●​ ServiceNow is Walmart’s primary operational tool \n●​ Used to: \n○​ Assign lines and claims \n○​ Track which agents worked on assigned lines or claims \n○​ Monitor volume inflow \n○​ Track SLA performance \n○​ Review data on closed lines and claims \nServiceNow serves as the source of truth for workload, productivity, and SLA compliance. \n \nIssue Reporting and Escalation \nIf an agent encounters any issue that prevents access to VDI, IC, or ServiceNow, the agent \nmust: \n1.​ Report the issue in the [VDI / PC Issue Tracker] \n2.​ Include the Start of Issue (SOI) with timestamp \n3.​ Report again once resolved, including the End of Issue (EOI) with timestamp \nThis ensures: \n●​ Accurate documentation \n●​ Proper time tracking \n●​ Visibility for operations and IT support\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nKey Reminders \n●​ VDI access is mandatory for IC and SNow usage \n●​ IC reflects client-side time and activity records \n●​ ServiceNow is the primary tool for assignment and SLA monitoring \n●​ All access issues must be logged with SOI and EOI to maintain accurate records\nLine Assignment/Latte Management\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n|Step-by-Step Process: Line Assignment (Manual) / LATTE \nManagement \nObjective \nTo ensure accurate and timely assignment of US, CA, and Pre-Item lines to properly \ntrained agents by prioritizing SLA urgency and real-time queue demand.US and CA \nqueues are treated with equal importance—priority is determined by which queue is \nmost urgent or at risk of SLA breach. \n \nSLA-Based Prioritization Guide \nUse the following SLA tiers to decide which lines to prioritize: \n Line Type  \nSLA Requirement \nTraining Required \nHigh Priority \nWithin 6 hours \nUS-trained / CA-trained \nP1 (US or CA) \nWithin 2 hours \nUS-trained / CA-trained \nP2 (US or CA) \nWithin 12 hours \nUS-trained / CA-trained \nP3 (US or CA) \nWithin 24 hours \nUS-trained / CA-trained \nP4 (US or CA) \nWithin 48 hours \nUS-trained / CA-trained \nPre-Items \nWithin 24 hours \nPre-Items-trained agents \n \nDashboard Link \n●​ ServiceNow Dashboard - Used to access updated links for each priority level \nand queue. \nAgent Requests and Assignment Procedure (Manual) Workflow Procedure \n1.​ Agents request lines via team chat: [WMT - Trust & Safety] \n2.​ Review current queue statuses (US, CA, and Pre-Items)\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n3.​ Identify which queue is most urgent based on SLA and volume \n4.​ Verify the agent’s training eligibility (US / CA / Pre-Items) \n5.​ Assign lines accordingly \n6.​ Confirm assignment via emoji reaction in chat\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \nEmoji Reactions to Confirm Assignment (Manual) \nOnce a line has been assigned, react to the agent’s message using one of the following \nemojis: \nLine Type \nEmoji Reaction \nMeaning \nUS Line \n \nUS line assigned \nCA Line \n \nCA line assigned \nPre-Items \n \nPre-item assigned \nAssigning Lines (Manual Assignment) \nLines can be assigned using either of the following conditions: \nSingle Assignment  \n●​ Double-click the empty “Assigned To” field \n●​ Type in the appropriate agent \nMultiple Assignment  \n●​ Highlight all empty “Assigned To” fields to be assigned \n●​ Double-click to bulk assign selected lines to an agent \nEnsure assignments match: \n●​ Agent training \n●​ Priority level \n●​ SLA urgency \nImportant Reminders\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n●​\nUS and CA queues have equal priority—always decide based on urgency \n●​\nDo not assign Pre-Items to non–Pre-Items-trained agents \n●​\nEmoji reactions act as confirmation and prevent duplicate assignments \n●​\nAlways monitor SLA risk before assigning lower-priority queues \n \nLATTE Volume Upload \n \nPurpose \nTo outline the standard process for uploading volume data into LATTE, ensuring \naccuracy, timeliness, and proper queue monitoring to support operational needs \nand SLA compliance. \n \nScope \nThis procedure applies to RTAs and authorized personnel responsible for: \n●​ Uploading US and CA volumes into LATTE \n●​ Monitoring queue health \n●​ Ensuring agent availability and responsiveness \n \nProcedure \n1. Download ServiceNow Volume \n●​ Access ServiceNow \n●​ Download the required volume file \n●​ Ensure the correct queue is selected:\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n○​ US \n○​ CA \n \n2. Upload Volume in LATTE Add screenshot \n \n●​ Open the LATTE Admin Dashboard \n●​ Navigate to Volume Import \n●​ Upload the downloaded ServiceNow volume file \n●​ Confirm upload completion and check for errors \n3. Monitor Queues and Agent Status\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \nQueue Monitoring \n●​ Go to Queue Statistics in the LATTE Admin Dashboard \n●​ Monitor: \n○​ Queue volume \n■​ RRTask Queue \n■​ Abstract Queue \nAgent Status Monitoring \n●​ Verify that all active agents are ONLINE in LATTE \n●​ If an agent is observed as IDLE: \n○​ Reach out to the agent via the Shoutout Channel \n○​ CC the agent’s Team Leader \n●​ If the agent is unresponsive: \n○​ File an entry in WFM Logs for proper documentation and follow-up \n \nUpload Frequency Guidelines\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nAdjust upload frequency based on volume conditions: \n●​ Low Volume \n○​ Upload every 30 minutes to 1 hour \n●​ High Volume \n○​ Upload every 1 to 2 hours \nAlways consider current queue demand and SLA exposure when determining upload \ntiming. \nTroubleshooting: Failed Volume Import \nIf a volume upload fails, perform the following steps: \nAccess Firebase – LATTE Database \n●​ Log in via Chrome using: \n○​ Email: wmt@ececontactcenters.com \n○​ Password: Walmart1234 \nClear Failed Import Records \n1.​ Open Firebase \n2.​ Navigate to: \n○​ import_jobs → latest upload → Delete document fields \n○​ admin_notifications → latest upload → Delete document fields \n3.​ Reattempt the volume upload in LATTE\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nImportant Reminders \n●​\nAlways verify that the correct US or CA file is uploaded \n●​\nEnsure agents are actively monitored during and after uploads \n●​\nPrompt escalation helps prevent SLA breaches \n●​\nDocument unresponsive agents through proper WFM channels\nRO Line Assignment\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n|Right Ownership (RO) Claim Assignment \nPurpose \nTo ensure timely and accurate assignment of claims to appropriate agents by \nfollowing SLA requirements, claim hierarchy, and brand-specific routing rules, \nwhile maintaining visibility of US and CA claim volumes. \n \nA.​ Claim Types and SLA Add screenshot \nAll claim types share the same SLA, but prioritization rules still apply. \nClaim Type \nSLA \nCounterfeit \n8 hours \nCopyright \n8 hours \nTrademark \n8 hours \nPatent \n8 hours \nImportant Note:​\nWhile all claim types have an 8-hour SLA, Counterfeit claims are always treated as higher priority \nwhen assigning. \n \nB.​ Start-of-Shift Responsibilities (RTA) \nAt the start of each shift, the RTA must: \n●​ Check RO claim volumes for both US and CA \n●​ Share the current claim count with the team \n●​ If there is no incoming volume: \n○​ Remind agents to work on: \n■​ Their pending claims \n■​ Any emails received\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nThis ensures productivity is maintained even during low-volume periods. \n \nC.​ Brand-Specific Assignment Rules \n●​ Apple brand claims \n○​ Must be assigned to Apple Dedicated agents only \n●​ StripeDevice claims \n○​ Automatically assigned to Teresa Lin (t0l013q) \nThese rules override general claim assignment flow. \n \nD.​ Agent Request and Compliance \n●​ All RO agents must request claims via: \n○​ For US - [Claim request Thread here ⬇️] \n○​ For CA - [CA Thread Claims] \n●​ Agents working on system-assigned claims must be issued an NTE for \nproper tracking and documentation \n \nE.​ Claim Assignment Prioritization \nWhen both US and CA queues are ready for assignment: \n●​ Treat US and CA as equal priority \n●​ Assign based on: \n○​ Claim hierarchy (Counterfeit first) \n○​ Created date (oldest first to prevent SLA breach) \n \nF.​ Claim Assignment Procedure \nTo assign a claim to an agent: \n1.​ Open the claim \n2.​ Update the “Locked To” field with the agent’s name\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n3.​ Click Save \n4.​ Select Start Review \n5.​ React to the agent’s request message with an emoji to notify them that a \nclaim has been assigned \nKey Reminders \n●​\nCounterfeit claims take priority despite equal SLAs. \n●​\nAlways consider the Created Date when assigning. \n●​\nFollow brand-specific routing without exception. \n●​\nEmoji reactions serve as confirmation of assignment. \n●​\nEnsure NTEs are issued when required for system-assigned claims.\nBULK\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n|Line Assignment (Bulk Process) \nPurpose / Scope \nThe purpose of this SOP is to define the workflow for the Real-Time Analyst (RTA) team \nwhen the CA Domain experiences a surge in Rule ID 3282 volume (ranging from \nthousands to 6-digit figures). This procedure ensures that bulk-authorized agents or \nautomated tools are utilized correctly to prevent SLA breaches. This applies to all RTAs \nand Operations Leadership managing the CA Domain. \n \nRoles & Responsibilities \n●​ Role: Real-Time Analyst (RTA) \n○​ Responsibility: Monitor real-time volume, identify 3282 spikes, and \ntrigger the initiation process by coordinating with the STL. \n●​ Role: Senior Team Lead (STL) \n○​ Responsibility: Approve the initiation of bulk processing and ensure the \n2–3 specified agents are available and assigned. \n●​ Role: Bulk-Authorized Agent \n○​ Responsibility: Execute high-speed completion of 3282 tasks using \nspecialized \"bulk complete\" system permissions. \n \nTools / Requirements \n●​ Item Risk Review Dashboard: To identify Rule ID volume spikes. \n●​ Latte Tool: For automated bulk importing/completion (used when 3282 is \nisolated). \n●​ Bulk Assignment Permission: Special access granted to the 2–3 specific \nagents.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nProcedure (Steps) \nStep 1: Volume Detection \nIdentify that Rule ID 3282 has reached \"Bulk\" status (thousands+). \n●​ Action: Analyze the current queue composition. Determine if the volume \nconsists exclusively of 3282 or if there is a mix of other Rule IDs. \nStep 2: Leadership Notification \nBefore taking action, the RTA must consult with the Senior Team Leader (STL). \n●​ Action: Inform the STL of the volume surge. \n●​ Required Info: Report the total volume and specify if it is \"Pure 3282\" or a \n\"Mixed Rule ID\" volume. If the volume only consist of 3282, ask for authorization \nto initiate bulk assignments to fasten completion. \nStep 3: Execution Path Selection \nBased on the STL\'s approval and volume type, follow the specific logic: \n●​ Scenario A (Mixed Volume): If 3282 is mixed with other Rule IDs, assign the \n3282 tasks specifically to the 2–3 bulk-authorized agents. \n●​ Scenario B (Pure 3282 Volume): If the volume contains only 3282 Rule IDs, do \nnot assign them to agents. Use the Latte Tool to import and complete the tasks. \nStep 4: Monitoring \n●​ Action: Track the queue until the 3282 volume returns to manageable levels \n(below \"bulk\" threshold). \nNote: The Latte Tool is the priority for volumes that are non-3282 Rule ID’s to \nensure the 2-3 agents can remain focused on the 3282 bulk assignments. \nExtraction Process: ​\n​\n​\nStep 1: Extract volume of pure 3282 Rule ID from CA P3 domain. Follow the \nFilter \nbelow:\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n​\n​\n​\nStep 2: After export, gather the names of the 2-3 agents provided by the STL for \nline assignment for the 3282 process. ​\n​\n​\nStep 3: For the distributing process, we should assure that the RRtasks \nextracted will be distributed equally among the agents. By using this process of \nextraction we could distribute close to equal amounts of RRtasks to the assigned \nagents. ​\n​\n​\n​\n​\nStep 4: After sum of RRtasks under an abstract, we should find the total of sum \nand divide it to how many agents that are assigned to the 3282 bulk completion.  \n \n5. Exceptions & Escalation \n●​ Issue: Authorized agents are offline or at capacity. \n○​ Action: Request the STL to designate temporary backup agents with bulk \npermissions. \n○​ Escalate To: STL.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n6. Quality Check / Expected Result \n●​ Expected Result: The 3282 volume is cleared rapidly without impacting the SLA \nof other Rule IDs in the CA Domain. \n●​ Verification: Confirm via the monitoring tool that the 3282 count is decreasing at \na rate faster than standard manual processing. \n \n7. Records / Outputs \n●​ Volume Recovery Report: Document the total 3282 volume cleared during the \nbulk session.\n🔴 Daily Data Downloads\nIR/Pre-Items Closed\nItem Review Closed \n1.​ Access ServiceNow \n○​ Use the provided ServiceNow link to download daily closed tasks. \n○​ Ensure the correct filters are applied: \n■​ \"Closed by\" field must not be empty. \n■​ \"Closed at\" must be set to yesterday’s date. \n○​ Note: Make sure that the time zone on ServiceNow is set to US Eastern. \n○​ Note: If the file exceeds 300,000 rows, the download must be split into two \nseparate files. \nColumns Needed \nItem Review Columns​\n​\n​\n​\n \n​\n​\nPre-Items Columns \n​\n \n2.​ Data Extraction \n○​ Extract the downloaded file from VDI. \n■​ Right Click on Columns - Export - CSV - Download \n○​ Export outside VDI through Taz. \n○​ Save the file to Google Drive. \n3.​ File Storage \n○​ Move the downloaded file to: \n■​ For US+CA - G:\\Shared drives\\Walmart Drive 2.0\\03 \nSKU\\005 SKU Closed PowerBI \n■​ For Pre-Items - G:\\Shared drives\\Walmart Drive 2.0\\06 \nPre-Items\\003 Pre Items Closed for PBI \n➔​Filters For US + CA \n◆​STATE ➡️ is ➡️ CLOSED COMPLETE \