bstract Product Id column → select Group by Abstract Product Id. \n \n \nSort the Created column in ascending order (arrow up). \n \n \n3. Check Requests in Cliq \nGo to the Trust and Safety Channel using this [#WMT - Trust & Safety]. \n \n \nFind the latest request without any reaction. \n \n \nReact with a waiting emoji (or similar) to acknowledge you’ll assign the line. \n \n \n4. Verify Agent Training \nAssign lines to the next capable / trained agent: \n \n \nUS-trained only: Assign lines from the US tenant (P1, P2, or P3 based on RTA’s priority). \n \n \nCross-trained (US + CA): Can handle any tenant.\nTo confirm CA training: \n \n \nOpen the Allowed CA Trained Agents sheet [CA Trained]. \n \n \nPress Ctrl + F, type the agent’s name. \n \n \nIf found → allowed for CA lines. If not → US only. \n \n \n5. Assign Lines \nIn the tab, go to the Assign To column. \n \n \nClick on a row marked “empty.” \n \n \nHold Ctrl, drag down, and highlight the desired number of lines. \n \n \nPress Enter, then type the agent’s name or VNUSERNAME. \n \n \nTip: Use Ctrl + Shift + ↓ to quickly highlight multiple rows. Then press Enter and enter the \nagent’s name or VNUSERNAME. \nPress Enter or click the check button to confirm. \n \n \n6. Confirm in Cliq \nReturn to the agent’s request in Cliq. \n \n \nMark the request to show you’ve assigned a line. \n \n \nRepeat for other agents as needed. \n \n \n \nImportant Notes\nP1: Contains OFAC lines → new hires are not allowed to answer. \n \n \nP3: Contains GLR → all agents may answer. \n \n \nAssign at least 35 lines per agent. \n \n \nIf an Abstract Product ID has more than 35 lines, assign it to only one agent. \n \n \n \nSupport \nIf you have questions, contact any RTA on shift for assistance.\nDaily Data Download\nStep-by-Step Process: Data Downloads \n(Walmart Drive 2.0) \n \nPurpose \nTo standardize the process of downloading and uploading operational data files into Walmart \nDrive 2.0 for accurate tracking and reporting. \n \n