er verifying that all the downloaded data is correct, send the file via \nemail. \n \n●​ The recipients are as follows: \nTO: \nPalash Manna - Vendor <Palash.Manna@walmart.com>, \nNorine Stearn <NStearn@walmart.com>, \nRicardo Vargas Ramirez <Ricardo.Vargas.Ramirez@walmart.com>, \nTania Das - Vendor <Tania.Das@walmart.com>,\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nSanjay Kumar - Vendor <Sanjay.Kumar2@walmart.com> \n​\nCC: \nJohn Mark Trias <jtrias@ececontactcenters.com>, \nRodolfo Luga <rluga@ececontactcenters.com>, \nEarl Maru Dave Rivera <erivera@ececontactcenters.com>, \nLemuel Ching <lching@ececontactcenters.com>, \nAnna Katrina Espino <akespino@ececontactcenters.com>, \nWendy Pastoral <wendy@ececontactcenters.com>, \nXerxes San Gregorio <xerxes@ececontactcenters.com>, \nLarry Bird Villaverde <lvillaverde@ececontactcenters.com>, \nSheena Rose Bolongaita <sbolongaita@ececontactcenters.com>, \nJulie Ann Irene Gumahad <jgumahad@ececontactcenters.com>, \nMary Grace Aganan <maganan@ececontactcenters.com>, \nJulhian Mark Cabarloc <jcabarloc@ececontactcenters.com>, \nEduard Compra <eduard.compra@ececontactcenters.com>, \nJohn Michael Vergara <john.vergara@ececontactcenters.com>, \nJabbar Minalang <jabbar.minalang@ececontactcenters.com>, \nShania Espina <sespina@ececontactcenters.com>, \nJomari Garces <jomari.garces@ececontactcenters.com>, \nPatricia Ann Bautista <patricia.bautista@ececontactcenters.com> \n \n●​ Body of the message \nHi Palash,​\nAttached herewith is the file for Item Review Forecasting May 17 - May 23, 2025. \nI have separate tabs for item SKU (Volume & Closed), Pre-item (Volume & \nClosed) and Right Owner US and CA Volume. Please expand the tabs if not \nvisible since it is sometimes hidden from Excel view. \nPlease note that the CIRT data is still truncated because the 150,000 download \nlimit issue has not yet been resolved. \nNote: PLEASE MAKE SURE TO ATTACH THE EXCEL FILE TO THE \nEMAIL BEFORE SENDING IT!\n🗓️ Scheduling management\nShift Bid / Swapping\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n|Workforce Management – Scheduling, Staffing, Shift Bid & Swapping \nScope \nSchedule creation, shift bid, schedule swaps, final schedule release Tools Used: Google \nSheets – Schedule Shell / Shift Bid / Master Schedule files Outputs: Approved Schedule \nShell, Initial Shift Assignments, Updated Swaps, Final Official Schedule. \n \nPurpose \nTo ensure accurate staffing coverage, fair shift allocation, and timely final schedule \nrelease. \n●​ Schedule Shell Creation (Staffing Requirement) Responsible Team: Scheduling \nDepartment / WFM Objective: To create a schedule shell based on \nclient-provided staffing requirements derived from forecasted volume. \n●​ Provide the forecasted volume to the client via WFM. \n●​ Convert volume into staffing requirements (agents per hour): \n●​ The client uses the forecasted volume to calculate required agents per hour. \n●​ The calculated staffing requirements are then given back to our RTAs/WFM \nteam. \n●​ Create the Schedule Shell showing: \n○​ hourly headcount requirements \n○​ required shift patterns \n■​ Validate: \n●​  staffing matches the client-provided requirements \n●​ coverage is balanced across all hours \n○​ Endorse the completed Schedule Shell to WFM/Operations. \n○​ Output: Approved Schedule Shell ready for shift assignment and bidding. \n \nShift Bid Process Objective: To accommodate the changing volume and demand of \nthe account, occasional team or schedule changes may occur, subject to client \napproval.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nProcedure \n1.​ Collect last 3 months Achieve Scores and latest PPH data.  (Use YTD Ranking \nsheet) \ni.​\nCreate a Stack Rank list: \n1.​ rank agents by Achieve Score \n2.​ use PPH as tie-breaker        ​\n \n2.​ Open Shift Bid window for 1 week. \n3.​ Agents submit their top preferred schedules using the Shift Bidding Form. \na.​ Placing the same schedule across all slots results in forfeiture of the bid, \nand the agent is placed at the bottom of scheduling priority. \nb.​ Failure to submit a bid within the allowable week results in assignment to \na random open schedule slot after all other bids are addressed. \n4.​ Monitor bidding progress daily and resolve issues. \n \nRules \n●​ Shift bidding priority is determined by the agent’s 3-month average scorecard \nscores. \n●​ Secured bids guarantee the preferred schedule if not claimed by a higher-ranked \nagent. Output: Initial list of assigned shifts based on bid results. \n●​ Schedule Swap Process Timeline: Immediately after Shift Bid closes Responsible \nTeam:  \n \nWFM Procedure: \n1.​ Announce Swap Window. \n2.​ Receive swap requests from both agents involved. \na.​ Validate that: \ni.​\nStaffing requirements are maintained \nii.​\nNo over/under-staffing occurs \n3.​ Approve valid swap requests and update master schedule. Swap Request Rules: \na.​    Both agents must submit the official Swap Request Form. \n4.​ Requests submitted by only one agent will not be processed. \n5.​ Approval is based on availability and operational requirements. Output: Updated \nschedule with all approved swaps incorporated.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nNote: The Responsible Team for the final schedule release is the WFM  \nFinal Schedule Procedure \n1.​ Lock final schedule after completion of swaps. \n2.​ Revalidate hourly coverage and total headcount. \n3.​ Release the final schedule to Operations and agents. Output: Official Final \nSchedule. \n4.​ Schedule Adjustments for Specific Needs \na.​ Agents who require schedule adjustments due to education or medical \nconditions must provide proper documentation. \nb.​ Adjustments are applied only to approved schedule options; creating \npersonal schedules is not allowed. \nc.​ Approval must come from Higher Operations (OM, AOM, STL). \nReminder: All schedules, shift bids, and swaps are in Eastern Standard Time (EST).\nFull-Time Equivalent (FTE)\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n|Scheduling for Internal Calibration (Full-Time Equivalent) \n \nPurpose / Scope \nThe purpose of this procedure is to identify the optimal time slots for internal calibration \nsessions based on agent headcount and production requirements. This ensures that \nLOB (Line of Business) specific calibration requests are met without compromising \nservice levels or dropping production shrinkage below acceptable thresholds during \npeak occupancy. \n​\n​\nRoles & Responsibilities \n●​ Role: RTA Analyst Responsibility: The analyst extracts schedules, identifies \npeak occupancy intervals, and sets calibration times within the WFM tools. \n●​ Role: Requestor Responsibility: The requester submits the initial ticket \nidentifying the specific LOB and/or agents needed for the session. \n●​ Role: Team Leader Responsibility: The Team Lead ensures agent adherence to \nthe finalized calibration schedule \n \nTools / Requirements \n●​ WFM Software (Transition Sheet, Workforce Rest) for schedule data. \n●​ Internal Ticketing System for request tracking, Zoho.  \n●​ FTE Scheduling Template (Excel or Google Sheets). \n \nProcedure (Steps) \nStep 1: Process the Headcount Request Ticket The process begins when a \nticket is received from a specific Line of Business (LOB) requesting headcount for an \ninternal calibration. Review the ticket to confirm the requested date and the number of \nagents involved using the template made.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n​\n​\n​\nStep 2: Initialize the Schedule Extraction Template Open the FTE template. \nThis step is critical for the filtering process, as it allows you to visualize the count of \nagents scheduled throughout the day. The template will serve as the primary tool to \ncalculate the impact on production.​\n​\n​\nStep 3: Extract Active Agent Schedules Access Workforce Rest or the \nscheduling sheet and extract the full schedule for all agents active on the date \nrequested.   \nStep 4: Identify Peak Occupancy and Maximum FTE Paste the extracted data \ninto the template. Analyze the intervals to find the peak occupancy, which is the specific \ntime of day when the highest number of agents are simultaneously on shift. Using the \nFTE template here is essential to see where the floor is most \"padded\" with staff. \nStep 5: Set the Calibration Schedule Once the maximum peak time is \nidentified, schedule the calibration during that window. Scheduling during peak \noccupancy ensures that pulling agents off the phones has the smallest possible impact \non shrinkage and does not cause a service level drop.​\n​\n \nNotes / Tips * Always ensure that the \"Maximum Peak\" does not conflict \nwith pre-planned lunches or large-scale training sessions already in the system. \n​\nExceptions & Escalation\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n●​ Issue: The requested headcount exceeds the available buffer during peak hours.​\nAction: Notify the LOB requestor that the headcount must be reduced.​\nEscalate: Operations \n●​ Issue: No clear \"Peak\" is visible due to high absenteeism.​\nAction: Deny the request for that specific date.​\nEscalate: Operations \n \nQuality Check / Expected Result \nThe task is successful when the calibration is scheduled during the highest FTE interval \nof the day, resulting in a stable shrinkage rate and no negative impact on the queue.\nTeam Movement/Employee Movement\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n|WFM TeamMovement \nPurpose \nTo ensure a standardized and organized approach in processing HR movements, \nthe Workforce RTA team will be responsible for submitting HR Movement Forms to \nZoho. This includes handling all employee transitions such as promotions, demotions, \nteam leader and senior team leader movements, floating statuses, and other personnel \nchanges within the operations team.​\n​\nPlease refer to this \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for HR Movement Notification Form_9/19/2…\n \nProcess \nStep 1: Operations Team Submission \n○​ Any employee movement request must be formally submitted by the \nOperations Team via a Workforce Management (WFM) ticket.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n○​ The WFM ticket must contain all necessary details, including employee \nname, ID, type of movement, effective date, and any required supporting \ndocuments. \n○​ The ticket serves as an official record of the request, ensuring \naccountability and tracking. \nStep 2: Verification by Workforce RTA​\n \n○​ The assigned RTA will review the submitted WFM ticket to verify \ncompleteness and accuracy. \n○​ If any details are missing or unclear, the RTA will coordinate with the \nrequestor to clarify and update the ticket before proceeding. \n○​ If the movement request is invalid or does not align with company policies, \nthe RTA will escalate to the Workforce Manager for further validation. \nStep 3: Submission to HR Movement Form​\n \n○​ Once validated, the RTA will input the details into the HR Movement Form \nin Zoho following standard processes. \n○​ After submission, the RTA must record the transaction and confirm with \nthe Operations Team that the request has been processed. \ni.​ Specific Cases: \n1.​ Change of Account: The receiving program’s RTA will \nprocess the movement. The Operations team must clearly \nindicate the new program and the effective date. \na.​ Wrong Account Assignment: If an employee is \nmoved to the incorrect program, the RTA must correct \nthe entry immediately and inform both the previous \nand receiving account teams. \n2.​ Change of Account (BENCH or Floating): The previous \nprogram’s RTA will process the movement, indicating the \nstart of floating status and its expected duration. \na.​ Floating Status Extended Beyond Expected \nDuration: If an employee remains on floating status \nlonger than the indicated period, RTA should follow up \nwith the Operations team for resolution. \nStep 4: Follow-Up & Confirmation\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n○​ The management team will process the movement request based on the \nsubmitted form. \n○​ RTAs are responsible for monitoring the status of each request and \nfollowing up if processing delays occur. \n○​ Once the management team finalizes the movement, RTAs will update the \nWFM ticket and close it for record-keeping purposes. \n \nSituational Events & Mitigations \n1.​ Incomplete or Incorrect Ticket Submission \n○​ If details in the WFM ticket are incomplete or inaccurate, the RTA will \nnotify the Operations Team immediately. \n○​ The movement request will not proceed until all required information is \nprovided. \n \n2.​ Urgent or Immediate Movements \n○​ For time-sensitive changes (e.g., same-day promotions, demotions, or \nfloating statuses), RTAs must escalate to Workforce Management for \npriority processing. \n○​ The Operations Team must indicate urgency in the WFM ticket for faster \nturnaround. \n \n3.​ Delayed Processing \n○​ If the management team does not update the movement within the \nexpected timeframe, the RTA must follow up within 48 hours. \n○​ Persistent delays will be escalated to leadership for resolution. \n \n4.​ Discrepancies in Movement Execution​\n \n○​ If an employee’s movement does not reflect correctly in payroll or records, \nRTAs will coordinate with the management team for corrections. \n○​ RTAs or operation teams must report discrepancies within 7 days of \nimplementation for timely adjustments.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \n5.​ Employee Disputes on Movement​\n \n○​ If an employee contests their movement status, RTAs will refer them to the \nOperations Team for clarification. \n○​ No adjustments will be made unless a new WFM ticket is submitted with \napproved corrections. \n6.​ Mass or Multiple Employee Movements​\n \n○​ For batch movements (e.g., restructuring or large promotions), RTAs must \nprepare in advance and coordinate closely with the management team. \n○​ A consolidated WFM ticket with all employees listed must be submitted to \nstreamline processing. \n \nCompliance & Accountability \n●​ RTAs are responsible for ensuring all movements are properly documented and \nprocessed according to company policy. \n●​ Operations Teams must adhere to the requirement of submitting a WFM ticket \nbefore any movement is processed. \n●​ Any failure to comply with this process will be subject to review and corrective \nactions as necessary.\n📃 Notice to Explain\nReturn to Work\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n|Return To Work (RTWO) \nIntroduction \nThis Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) provides a comprehensive framework \nfor monitoring employee attendance, identifying violations, and managing the \npreparation, review, and filing of disciplinary notices. It ensures a consistent and \ncompliant approach to addressing No Call, No Show (NCNS) and other \nattendance-related issues, guiding the process from initial monitoring through final \ndocumentation and system submission. Serving as a central reference for Operations, \nReal-Time Analysts, and Human Resources, this SOP promotes accurate, fair, and \ntimely handling of attendance concerns while maintaining proper records and supporting \naudit readiness. \n \nPurpose \nThe purpose of this SOP is to standardize the monitoring of attendance, establish \nclear criteria for identifying NCNS and consecutive absences, ensure accurate and \nconsistent preparation of NTE and NOD documents, and provide a structured process \nfor administrative hearings and proper filing in Zoho. It promotes fairness, transparency, \nand compliance with company policies, ensuring that attendance-related disciplinary \nactions are timely, documented, and defensible. \nA.​ Monitoring \nThis section outlines the process for monitoring agent time logs to ensure accurate \ntracking of time-in and time-out records. The primary objective is to identify agents with \nabsences and determine whether those absences qualify as No Call, No Show \n(NCNS).\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \n \nCriteria: \n●​ Employees who incur NCNS absences for three (3) consecutive days are \nsubject to evaluation and possible sanctions if a violation is confirmed. \n \n \nManual Monitoring Procedure \n●​ Access Zoho Time Logs \n○​ Navigate to Zoho Time Logs. \n○​ Search using the following criteria (code) \n■​ Account: Walmart \n■​ Date Range: Three (3) consecutive days \n■​ Absent: Greater or equal to: 8 \n \n \n○​ For subsequent checks, include the previous three (3) days and the \nfollowing three (3) days to ensure continuity. \n■​ Example: \n●​ Initial check: January 1–3 \n●​ After three days, recheck using: January 1–6​\nContinue the same rolling date range for succeeding\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nreviews.​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n \n \n●​ Download Required Data \n​\n \n○​ Download the following columns:​\n \n■​ Employee Number \n■​ Employee Name \n■​ Date(s) of Absence \n■​ Absence Value(s)​\n \n●​ Update the Monitoring Sheet \n○​ Open the downloaded file. \n○​ Copy the required columns and paste \nthem into the Monitoring Sheet.​\n \n●​ Review in RTWO Pivot Monitoring \n○​ Go to the RTWO PIVOT MONITORING tab.​\nIdentify employees with multiple consecutive absences. \n○​ Filter employees with two (2) or more consecutive absence counts. \n○​ These employees are subject to further review to determine the reason for \ntheir absences. \n \n●​ Absent Verification Process\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n○​ The Absent Verification Process ensures that all employee absences are \nproperly validated and documented before determining if they constitute a \nviolation. \n○​ Determine whether the employee has provided sufficient evidence to \nsupport the absence as valid. \n \n○​ Verification Steps \n1.​ Review Time Logs – Confirm the employee’s recorded time-in and \ntime-out for the relevant dates. \n2.​ Check APS (Admin) – Verify administrative records for any \napproved leave or prior notifications. \n3.​ Verify Attendance Notifications – Ensure any formal notifications \nof absence have been submitted and recorded. \n4.​ Review Emails – Check for relevant email communications \nregarding the absence. \n5.​ Line of Sight (LOS) Notifications – Confirm any messaging app \nnotifications under company systems that may provide context or \njustification for the absence. \n \n●​ Issuance of NTE​\n \n○​ If the absences are determined to be intentional or unjustified, the \nemployee will be issued a Notice to Explain (NTE) for further clarification. \nImportant Reminder \nConsecutive absences are counted based on actual business \ndays missed, regardless of whether they overlap with rest days, vacation \nleave (VL), or voluntary time off (VTO). If an employee is absent on \nconsecutive business days, an NTE must be issued. \nB.​ NTE / NOD Document Preparation \nBREW Tool\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nThe BREW Tool is the system used for the preparation of Notice to Explain (NTE) and \nNotice of Decision (NOD) documents. The tool generates standardized documents by \npopulating \npredefined \nplaceholders \nwith \nemployee \ndata, \nensuring accuracy, \nconsistency, and compliance with documentation standards. \nRelated Article: Introducing BREW Tool  \nProcess Integration \nOnce employees subject to disciplinary action have been identified, the BREW Tool \nmust be used to generate the required documentation. \n1.​ Employee Identification \n○​ Confirm the list of employees who are required to receive an NTE. \n○​ Encode the complete and accurate employee details into the BREW Tool \nbackend sheet. \n \n2.​ Document Generation \n○​ After all required fields in the backend sheet have been completed, \nproceed to Step 2 of the BREW Tool. \n○​ Generate the NTE or NOD document. \n○​ Download the generated file. \n○​ Conduct a thorough quality check to verify accuracy, completeness, and \nproper formatting.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n \n3.​ Manual Review and Adjustments \n○​ The BREW Tool is currently undergoing enhancements and does not yet \noperate at full capability. \n○​ Required images are not automatically inserted, and certain information \nmay not be fully consolidated. \n○​ Manual editing is required, particularly in the highlighted sections within \nthe body of the document, to ensure correctness and clarity. \nAdministrative Hearing Scheduling \n1.​ Request for Administrative Hearing Details \n○​ The second page of the NTE/NOD document must include the \nadministrative hearing date and meeting link. \n○​ To obtain this information, submit a scheduling request via the HR/RTA \nChannel on Zoho Cliq. \nRequest Format​\n​\n​\nName of the Employee: (Name) \nCurrent Shift: (e.g., 10 00 EST - 21 00 EST) \nRest Days: (e.g., Sat - Sun) \n2.​ HR Notification \n○​ Ensure the appropriate HR personnel are included in the request: \n■​ Manila: HR May Trianes\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n■​ Dumaguete: PR Glenn or PR Arleigh​\n \n3.​ Calendar Scheduling and System Upload \n○​ Upon receipt of the administrative hearing schedule: \n■​ Create a meeting invitation in Google Calendar. \n■​ Include the following required participants: \n■​ Operations Manager (OM) \n■​ Assistant Operations Manager (AOM) \n■​ Site Team Lead (STL) \n■​ Human Resources (HR) \n■​ Real-Time Analysts (RTAs) \n■​ The concerned employee \n■​ The employee’s Team Leader (TL)​\n \n​\nRelated Article: How to Plot Admin Hearing In Google Calendar \n○​ After the meeting is scheduled, upload the calendar invitation to Zoho for \nrecord-keeping and compliance tracking. \nC. Filing Procedure \n1.​ Access the Zoho Sign Request Form \n○​ Navigate to Zoho. \n○​ From the HR sidebar, select Zoho Sign Request Form.​\n \n2.​ Complete the Required Information \n○​ Accurately fill in all required fields in the form. \n○​ Ensure that the information provided matches the details in the finalized \ndocument.​\n \n3.​ Submit the Request \n○​ Review all entries for accuracy and completeness. \n​\nRelated Article: Issuance of Notice to Explain (NTE) and Notice of Decision \n(NOD)\nUnauthorize Break Extension\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n|Unauthorize Break Extension \nMonitoring  \nThe Monitoring of Unauthorized Break Extensions ensures that all employees \nare accounted for and that any unauthorized extensions of non-productive auxiliary time \nare identified. Appropriate sanctions may be applied to correct unproductive behavior, in \naccordance with the guidelines outlined in the company handbook. \n \n \nTo monitor, the employee behavior is compared against the established criteria to \ndetermine if any violations have occurred. \nCriteria: \n●​ Unauthorized breaks or extensions of scheduled breaks five (5) times within one \n(1) month, or \n●​ Accumulated overbreaks totaling sixty (60) minutes within one (1) month, \nwhichever occurs first. \nMonitoring is typically conducted at the end of each month. However, to prevent delays \nin addressing infractions, checks should also be performed weekly. Employees who \nmeet or exceed the criteria during these checks will be issued a Notice to Explain \n(NTE) in a timely manner.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nA.​ Reviewing Process \nTo identify employees who have violated the criteria for unauthorized break extensions, \nthe PBI Report Dashboard for Overbreak must be refreshed. This review should be \nconducted every Sunday. \nOnce the employees who meet the criteria are identified: \n1.​ Transfer Data – Download the relevant data from the PBI Dashboard and \ntransfer it to the Unauthorized Break Extension Monitoring Sheet. Copy the data \ninto the designated tab for unauthorized break extensions.​\n \n2.​ Update Employee List – Ensure that all employees who meet the criteria are \nlisted in the monitoring sheet.​\n \n3.​ NTE/NOD Preparation – Once the list is updated, begin the process of creating \nNotice to Explain (NTE) or Notice of Decision (NOD) documents for the identified \nemployees. \n \nB. NTE / NOD Document Preparation \nBrew Tool \nThe BREW Tool is the system used for the preparation of Notice to Explain (NTE) and \nNotice of Decision (NOD) documents. The tool generates standardized documents by \npopulating \npredefined \nplaceholders \nwith \nemployee \ndata, \nensuring accuracy, \nconsistency, and compliance with documentation standards. \nRelated Article: Introducing BREW Tool  \nProcess Integration \nOnce employees subject to disciplinary action have been identified, the BREW Tool \nmust be used to generate the required documentation. \n1.​ Employee Identification \n○​ Confirm the list of employees who are required to receive an NTE.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n○​ Encode the complete and accurate employee details into the BREW Tool \nbackend sheet. \n \n2.​ Document Generation \n○​ After all required fields in the backend sheet have been completed, \nproceed to Step 2 of the BREW Tool. \n○​ Generate the NTE or NOD document. \n○​ Download the generated file. \n○​ Conduct a thorough quality check to verify accuracy, completeness, and \nproper formatting. \n \n3.​ Manual Review and Adjustments \n○​ The BREW Tool is currently undergoing enhancements and does not yet \noperate at full capability. \n○​ Required images are not automatically inserted, and certain information \nmay not be fully consolidated. \n○​ Manual editing is required, particularly in the highlighted sections within \nthe body of the document, to ensure correctness and clarity.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nC. Filing Procedure \n1.​ Access the Zoho Sign Request Form \n○​ Navigate to Zoho. \n○​ From the HR sidebar, select Zoho Sign Request Form.​\n \n2.​ Complete the Required Information \n○​ Accurately fill in all required fields in the form. \n○​ Ensure that the information provided matches the details in the finalized \ndocument.​\n \n3.​ Submit the Request \n○​ Review all entries for accuracy and completeness. \n4.​ Notice of Decision \n○​ All responses to Notice to Explain (NTE) must be carefully reviewed. \nEnsure that any decisions derived from the NTE responses and included \nin the Notice of Decision (NOD) are accurate, consistent, and in full \ncompliance with company policies and established criteria. This step is \ncritical to maintain fairness, transparency, and proper documentation of all \ndisciplinary actions. \n​\nRelated Article: Issuance of Notice to Explain (NTE) and Notice of Decision \n(NOD)\n🪣 RTA Outside Task\n⌛ IC request stamps\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n|IC Request Stamps \n​\nProcedure \n​\nBreaks/Timelogs - To ensure accurate recording, correction, and approval of employee \nbreaks and time logs through a controlled IC request stamp process, maintaining \ncompliance and audit readiness. \nScope: Applies to all employees ICs involved in timekeeping, including: \n●​ Missed punches \n●​ Incorrect break entries \n●​ Manual time log adjustments \n \nStep 1: Submit the Request \nAgents must submit their request for an IC timestamp in the IC SCREENSHOT \nREQUESTS thread in Cliq. The request must follow the template below: \n​\nIC REQUEST TEMPLATE \nRequesting IC Stamp:​\nDate:​\nShift:​\nReason: \nStep 2: Access IC Data Download \nOpen IC, then navigate to Data Download if requesting a screenshot of break \nlogs. \nStep 3: Generate the Agent State Log \n1.​ Search for Agent State Log (350083). \n2.​ Set the Date Range based on the date for which the agent is requesting the \nscreenshot. \n3.​ Set the Start Time to 12:00 AM and the End Time to 11:59 PM. \n4.​ Select “Comma Separated” as the Export Format.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n5.​ Ensure “Include Field Names” is checked. \n6.​ Click Download.​\n \nStep 4: Export the File Outside VDI \nTo ensure file accessibility, the exported file must be downloaded outside the \nVDI. You may send the file to TAZ Bot(Cliq), then download it outside the VDI, as the \nfile is in Excel format. \n​\nStep 5: Clean and Format the File \nOnce the file is downloaded, open it and remove or delete any unnecessary \ncolumns. Ensure that the following columns are retained:  \n●​ Agent Name \n●​ Start Date \n●​ Outstate \n●​ End Date \nNote: Confirm that the date and time format is set to m/d/yyyy h:mm:ss.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n​\n​\nStep 6: Filter the Data \nFilter the data based on the agent’s timestamp request to locate the relevant \nentries. \n \n \nLogin/Logout​\n​\nStep 1: Submit the Request \n \nAgents must submit their request for an IC timestamp in the IC Screenshot \nRequests thread in Cliq. The request must follow the template below: \n \nRequesting IC Stamp: \nDate: \nShift: \nReason: \n \nStep 2: Access IC Prebuilt Reports \n \n●​ Open IC and navigate to Prebuilt Reports. \n●​ Select Agent Time Card. \n \nStep 3: Configure Report Parameters \n \n●​ Set the Date Range based on the date for which the agent is requesting the \nscreenshot. \n●​ Set the Start Time to 12:00 AM and the End Time to 11:59 PM.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n●​ Under Agents, click the + button to add the specific agent’s name. \n●​ After adding the agent, click Done, then Run Report.​\n​\n \n​\nStep 4: Capture and Send Data \n \n●​ Take a screenshot of the report data. \n●​ Send the screenshot to the agent who submitted the request.​\n​\n🪣 Vacation Leave Slot Update\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n|VL Slot Update \nPurpose \nTo determine the number of available Vacation Leave (VL) slots per day for \nthe upcoming month, ensuring proper workforce coverage, timely filing by agents, and \naccurate application in Zoho. \n \nFrequency \n●​ Performed two (2) weeks before next month. \n●​ Completed at least 1 week before the start of the next month \n \nProcedure \nStep 1. Access Attendance Tracker \n●​ Open the current month’s attendance tracker \n●​ Use it as a reference to generate or validate the next month’s attendance \ntracker \nStep 2. Validate Agent Schedules \n●​ Review and track each agent’s: \n○​ Scheduled workdays \n○​ Rest days \n●​ Ensure all Rest Days (RD) schedules from the Transition Sheet are correctly \nreflected for the upcoming month. \nStep 3. Calculate Available VL Slots \n●​ Locate the VL computation formula below the attendance tracker \n●​ The standard calculation is: \n○​ 5% of the total number of agents scheduled per day \n●​ The resulting value represents the total VL slots available per day\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nNote: While the baseline is 5%, Operations leadership (STLs and higher) may \noverride the computed number of slots when necessary. \nStep 4. Consolidate VL Slot Data \n●​ Extract daily VL slot availability for the entire upcoming month \n●​ Copy the data into a separate Excel file \n●​ Validate: \n○​ Date accuracy \n○​ Correct slot totals per day \nStep 5. Submit for Zoho Application \n●​ Send the finalized Excel file to Imee Compra \n●​ This enables the application of VL slot availability in Zoho \n \nTimeliness and Filing Considerations \n●​ Timely submission is critical to prevent late VL filings by agents \n●​ VL requests must be filed: \n○​ At least 7 days before the intended leave date \n○​ No more than 30 days in advance \n●​ Delays in slot uploads may restrict agent filing eligibility and cause compliance \nissues \n \nKey Notes and Reminders \n●​ VL slots are primarily based on 5% daily workforce availability \n●​ Overrides may be applied by Operations (STLs and above) \n●​ Accuracy and timeliness directly impact agent leave filing compliance \n●​ Always double-check data prior to submission\n🪣 SNW Issue Tracker\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Walmart Support \n|Reporting Issue on ServiceNow \nPurpose / Scope \n●​ Accurate reporting of system or workflow issues \n●​ Timely transfer of affected items to the appropriate RTA personnel \n●​ Clear accountability and traceability of reported issues \n \nRoles & Responsibilities \nRole \nResponsibility \nRTA (Reporting RTA) \nIdentify affected items, complete the reporting form, transfer \nitems, and coordinate confirmation \nOnshift RTA \nReceive transferred items and validate successful handoff \nRTA \nLead \n/ \nSupervisor \nEscalation point for unresolved or repeated issues \n \n3. Tools / Requirements \n●​ SNW (System Navigation Workspace) – for item review and transfer \n●​ Google Forms – official reporting channel \n●​ Internal Chat Tool (e.g., Cliq, Slack, Teams, or equivalent) – for coordination \nand confirmation \n●​ Valid System Access – RTA-level permissions \n \n4. Procedure (Steps) \nStep 1: Identify Items to Be Reported \nContinuously monitor assigned queues, dashboards, or task lists. Identify items \nthat meet any of the following criteria:\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n●​ Non-disappearing items​\nItems that remain in the queue (Bucket) despite expected completion or \nresolution. \n●​ Erroring items​\nItems showing system errors, failed processing, or abnormal behavior preventing \naction. \n●​ Already completed but non-actionable items​\nItems marked as done or completed but still appearing and cannot be acted \nupon. \nEnsure the item truly meets one of the above criteria before proceeding to \nreporting. \nStep 2: Validate the Item Status \nBefore reporting: \n●​ Recheck item details and timestamps \n●​ Confirm the issue persists after refresh or basic troubleshooting \n●​ Verify that the item is not pending action from another team or system delay \nIf the issue remains unresolved, proceed to reporting. \nStep 3: Report the Item via Google Form \n1.​ Access the official reporting form using the link below:​\nhttps://docs.google.com/forms/d/1obH5RtGQemSbomqD_n2pMJeVFen1d7b_Ep\nxcjwRDe3M/viewform \n2.​ Complete all required fields accurately, importantly; \n○​ Name of the agent reporting \n○​ Item identifier (ItemId) \n○​ Screenshot \n○​ Brief description of the issue \n3.​ Review entries for accuracy. \n4.​ Submit the form. \nStep 4: Transfer the Item in SNW \n1.​ Open the affected item in SNW. \n2.​ Initiate a transfer action. \n3.​ Transfer the item to any On-shift RTA.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \n○​ If no on-shift RTA is available, transfer to:​\nRTA Maykel VN Username: John Vergara – Vendor (vn5774u) \n4.​ Ensure the transfer is completed successfully in the system. \n5.​ In case the item is able to be transferred, please contact RTA immediately. \nStep 5: Confirm Successful Transfer \n1.​ Contact the receiving RTA via Cliq. \n2.​ Confirm that: \n○​ The item is visible on their end \n○​ Ownership has been successfully transferred \n3.​ Retain confirmation for reference if follow-up is required. \n \nNotes / Tips \n●​ Always submit the Google Form before or immediately after transferring the \nitem. \n●​ Use clear and concise descriptions to avoid back-and-forth clarifications. \n●​ Do not transfer items without proper reporting unless instructed by an RTA Lead. \n \nExceptions & Escalation \nIssue \nAction \nEscalate To \nProblem with the items on \nSNW \nTry to take action via Allowing or \nBlocking the Item, Issue persist \nTeam Lead First \nGoogle Form is inaccessible \nTake screenshots and document \ndetails \nRTA \nItem cannot be transferred in \nSNW \nAttempt retry and document \nerror \nRTA / Team Lead \nReceiving RTA cannot see \nthe item \nReconfirm transfer details \nRTA \nRepeated \noccurrence \nof \nsame issue \nLog and flag as recurring \nRTA\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \n \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/\n\nSOP NTE File Creator \nLast Updated : 06.17.2025 \nImportant Links: \nNTE Generation \nZoho Sign Request Data \n \nPROCESS OVERVIEW \n \n \n \n \n \nI.\nNTE Generation \nFigure 1.0 shows the View Employees (NTE Generation) Report. \n \nFigure 1.0 \nThe Report above shows the latest APE points of each employee. Only those \nemployees with APS points greater than or equal to eight will be displayed. Creating \nease in monitoring employees whose points need attention. \nTo start creating NTE file for the selected employee, click Create NTE Record \n \nNTE Creation \nHR Approval \nEmployee Signing \nCompleted\nbutton.  \nNOTE: Once you clicked the create NTE button, it will create a record in Zoho Sign Request \nData. Kindly check records to avoid duplication. \nFigure 1.2 illustrates the Zoho Sign Request Data Report. \n \nFigure 1.2 \nClick the Create NTE file button to open the file Creator. Figure 1.3 illustrates the \nNTE File Creator. \n \nFigure 1.3\nDocument Details has two types of templates:  \n●\nSection 10: \n○\nRegular NTE \n○\nNTE + Admin Hearing \n○\nNTE + Admin Hearning + RTWO \n○\nNTE + Admin Hearing + Preventive Suspension \n●\nAPS Related \n○\nNTE Infractions of Company Rules \n \nThe system lets the user to input date start and date end of APS points. The app \nwill then display below the preview of the table containing the dates, APS points and \nrollback points. Please see figure 1.4. \n \nFigure 1.4 \nFigure 1.5 shows the CC list management. This allows the user to add email addresses \nto be added to the default CC list of the document to be generated. \nIn case of an incorrect default CC list or an outdated list has been loaded, the user can \nremove the loaded default cc list in the Add CC section. The removed default email will \nstill be shown in the CC list for account review purposes.\nFigure 1.5 \nOnce ready, the user can click submit and the application will automatically \ndownload the generated NTE file in their Local machine. \nFigure 1.6 shows the status of the document on a successful submission. The \ndocument status will be set to \"Pending\". \n \nFigure 1.6 \nThe sender will then receive a notification that the file is ready for reviewing. See \nFigure 1.7. The notification includes a link that will redirect the user to the said record.\nFIgure 1.7 \nOn Figure 1.8 the uploaded document will be showed in the Generated File \nField of the report. \n \nFigure 1.8 \nThe user can now review the document and proceed with clicking the \ncreate/update document button. \nFigure 1.9 shows the Generate NTE form with the Update Type Form indicated on \nthe upper right corner. \nThe user can select from the following Statuses: \n \n●\nPending \n●\nFor Approval \n●\nFor Signing \n●\nSigned \n●\nRejected \n●\nFor Deletion\nFigure 1.9 \nIf there are no errors in the generated document, the submitter can now change \nthe status to \"For Approval\".  \nAn approver must be entered before proceeding; otherwise, the app will prompt \nthe user. \nThe Approver will then be notified that the file should be approved before it will \nproceed to the employee. Once the File has no errors, the approver can now select \"FOR \nSIGNING\" status. \nThe CC list will receive a receipt of the email in their inbox. \nAn icon with the label of NOT VIEWED indicates that the document has not been \nviewed yet by the recipient and will changed to VIEWED in green color to indicate that \nthe recipient has clicked links that was sent thru his/her registered zoho email, cliq \nnotification and ECE Track Dashboard. \nDocument ID can be found under the Update Document Title at the top right part \nof the form. \nFigure 1.10 shows the notification sent to the employee. This indicates that the\nNTE file has been approved and ready to be signed the recipient. \n \nFigure 1.10 \nThe user can click the open button and will be redirected to the record of the file. \nAn email will also be sent to the employee\'s mailbox. Once the Link in the email or the \nopen button in the cliq notification is clicked, it will redirect the user to the view of the \nNTE document and will tag the document as VIEWED. \nFigure 1.11 show the email sent to the employee for NTE document. \n \nFigure 1.11 \nFigure 1.12 shows the My NTE Page. The user can view and add response on the \nNTE document though this view. \n \nFigure 1.12 \nThe user can view the NTE document by clicking the file in the Generated NTE \nfield. Once read, the user can now reply by clicking the Add Response button. The \nbutton will open a form and once response is added, the user can click submit. See\nFigure 1.13. \n \nFigure 1.13 \nThe appover and the submitter will be notified once the file with the employee\'s \nsigniture and response is generated. \n \n \nFigure 1.14\n\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC. \n33F Robinsons Summit Center \n 6783 Ayala Avenue, Makati City 1226 \nMetro Manila \n \nwww.ececonsultinggroup.com \nSOP Dashboard - Admin \nWhat this covers \n●\nCreating/maintaining the SOP Group folder in WorkDrive (one folder per \nApp/Group). \n●\nUploading SOP files so employees can view them from the SOP Dashboard. \n●\nLocking down edits so only authorized users can create/sync folders or publish \nfiles. \nWho should do this \n●\nSOP Admins or System Admins with access to ECE Time Tracker and WorkDrive \n(optional). \nPrerequisites \n●\nYou can access the report: All Sop Groups. \n●\nYou know the Group/App name you’re creating an SOP folder for (e.g., ExTra PH, \nECETrack). \n●\nYou know which parent WorkDrive category to use in WD_Folder: \n■\nSupport – standard (default) support knowledge base \n■\nGeneral – company-wide general SOPs \nNote: On submit, the system creates the folder in WorkDrive and stores its ID in \nWD_Folder_ID automatically.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC. \n33F Robinsons Summit Center \n 6783 Ayala Avenue, Makati City 1226 \nMetro Manila \n \nwww.ececonsultinggroup.com \nWhere to start \n1. Open the All Sop Groups report: \n■\nhttps://creatorapp.zoho.com/ececonsultinggroup/ece-time-\ntracker/?#Report:All_Sop_Groups \n2. Confirm you can see the existing rows (e.g., Group, WD_Folder, WD_Folder_ID). \nCreate a new SOP Group (new row) \n1. Open the All Sop Groups report: \n■\nhttps://creatorapp.zoho.com/ececonsultinggroup/ece-time-\ntracker/?#Report:All_Sop_Groups \n2. Click the ➕ (plus) icon at the top‑right of the report to open the SOP Group form. \n3. In the form (see field screenshot): \n■\nWD_Folder (required): Select Support or General. \n■\nGroup (required): Type the exact App/Group name (e.g., ExTra PH, \nECETrack).\n \n4. Click Submit. \n5. After a few seconds, return to the report and verify your new row: \n■\nWD_Folder shows your chosen category. \n■\nWD_Folder_ID is populated (folder created successfully). If it’s blank, see \nTroubleshooting below.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC. \n33F Robinsons Summit Center \n 6783 Ayala Avenue, Makati City 1226 \nMetro Manila \n \nwww.ececonsultinggroup.com \nTips \n●\nUse the report search to ensure the Group doesn’t already exist before adding a \nnew one. \n●\nGroup names should be unique and match the app/team naming convention \nexactly. \nVerify the setup (very important) \n●\nReturn to the All Sop Groups report and find your newly added Group. \n●\nCheck that WD_Folder shows your chosen category. \n●\nConfirm WD_Folder_ID is not empty. \n●\nIf present, the folder was created successfully. \n●\nIf empty after ~10–30 seconds, see Troubleshooting below. \nEdit or update an existing Group \n●\nNo edits allowed after creation. Once a Group is created, both Group and \nWD_Folder are locked and cannot be changed. \nIf something is wrong \n●\nDo not try to edit the record or create a duplicate. \n●\nSubmit a support ticket to request an admin action (retire/delete the incorrect \nGroup and create a new one): \n■\nRequest Portal → Zoho Support Ticketing (include the exact Group name \nand desired WD_Folder: General or Support). \nImportant \n●\nAvoid duplicate Group names. Use the search bar to confirm the Group does not \nalready exist before adding a new one. \n●\nWD_Folder_ID is fixed after creation and is tied to the WorkDrive folder created \nfor that Group.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC. \n33F Robinsons Summit Center \n 6783 Ayala Avenue, Makati City 1226 \nMetro Manila \n \nwww.ececonsultinggroup.com \nHow this works (for admins) \n●\nOn submit, the workflow uses WD_Folder to select the parent WorkDrive folder \n(e.g., Support vs General). \n●\nThe script then creates the folder, and saves its resource ID to WD_Folder_ID. \n●\nLater automations (e.g., SOP uploads) use WD_Folder_ID to publish files and \ngenerate embed/permalink links. \nTroubleshooting – SOP Group \n1. WD_Folder_ID is blank \n●\nRefresh the report. If still blank: \n■\nEnsure WD_Folder was set correctly. \n■\nConfirm your WorkDrive connection (work_drive_zoho_files) is active. (ask \nthe dev) \n■\nTry editing and re‑submitting the record. \n2. “Duplicate group” or validation error \n●\nSearch the report for an existing row with the same Group. If found, do not create \na duplicate. Users cannot edit existing records — contact the dev team or submit \na Zoho Support Ticketing request to retire/adjust the existing row. \n3. Permission or API error \n●\nYou might lack WorkDrive create permissions in the destination parent folder. \nContact the dev team or submit a Zoho Support Ticketing. \n4. Wrong parent folder \n●\nUsers cannot edit this field. Do not modify the record. \n●\nSubmit a Zoho Support Ticketing request or contact the dev team to move the \nSOP Group to the correct parent (change control required).\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC. \n33F Robinsons Summit Center \n 6783 Ayala Avenue, Makati City 1226 \nMetro Manila \n \nwww.ececonsultinggroup.com \nCreate a new SOP (File Upload) \nPrerequisites \n●\nThe target SOP Group already exists (created via All Sop Groups above). \n●\nYour document is a PDF (only PDF is allowed). \nSteps \n1. Open the All Sops report: \n■\nhttps://creatorapp.zoho.com/ececonsultinggroup/ece-time-\ntracker/?#Report:All_Sops \n2. Click the ➕ (plus) icon at the top‑right to open the SOP form. \n3. Fill the fields: \n■\nTitle (required): Short, clear name of the SOP. \n■\nSOP Access (required): Choose General or Support. \n■\nSOP Group (required): Select the correct Group for this SOP. (If the list is \ndisabled, pick SOP Access first.) If the Group you need isn’t listed, go back \nand create it in All Sop Groups. \n■\nDocument (required): \n●\nUpload the PDF file (only upload files of size up to 250MB).\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC. \n33F Robinsons Summit Center \n 6783 Ayala Avenue, Makati City 1226 \nMetro Manila \n \nwww.ececonsultinggroup.com \n \n \n4. Click Submit. \n5. Verify in the report that your new SOP appears. (Back‑end automation uploads \nthe PDF to the Group’s WorkDrive folder and stores references as configured.) \nNotes \n●\nDo not create duplicate SOPs for the same title and group. Use search first. \n●\nIf the wrong group/access was selected, submit a support ticket to request \ncorrection (editing may be restricted).\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC. \n33F Robinsons Summit Center \n 6783 Ayala Avenue, Makati City 1226 \nMetro Manila \n \nwww.ececonsultinggroup.com \nVerify the setup (very important) \nAfter submitting, open All Sops and confirm: \n●\nThe new SOP row is visible with the correct Title, SOP Access, and SOP Group. \n●\nThe file opens/preview works from the row’s link/button (permalink/embed). \n●\nAny WorkDrive reference fields (e.g., Resource_ID, Permalink/Embed URL) are \npopulated. \n●\nThe file name and size look correct. \nIf any of these are missing or broken, see Troubleshooting below. \nEdit or update an existing SOP (SOP – File upload) \nAllowed change: You can replace the PDF (Document). Title, SOP Access, and SOP \nGroup are locked after creation. \nSteps to replace the PDF: \n1. In All Sops, open the target SOP row. \n2. Click Edit. \n3. In Document, choose the new PDF. \n4. Click Submit. \nNotes \n●\nThe system replaces the existing file in WorkDrive (keeps the same Group folder). \nLinks remain valid. \n●\nDo not change the Title to create a “new” version; use file replacement instead. \n●\nIf Access/Group is wrong, submit a support ticket for admin correction.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC. \n33F Robinsons Summit Center \n 6783 Ayala Avenue, Makati City 1226 \nMetro Manila \n \nwww.ececonsultinggroup.com \nHow this works (for admins) \n●\nOn creation, the workflow looks up the Group’s WD_Folder_ID and uploads the \nPDF to that WorkDrive folder. \n●\nThe script publishes/updates permissions as configured and saves references \n(e.g., resource_id, permalink/embed URL). \n●\nOn edit (file replacement), the script updates the WorkDrive file (or re‑uploads \nand updates references) without changing the Group folder. \n●\nVersion history can be tracked in WorkDrive if enabled. \nTroubleshooting – SOP File Upload \n1. Upload blocked: “PDF only”\nConvert your document to PDF and re‑upload. \n2. SOP doesn’t show a link / link broken\nRefresh the report; if still missing, check the Group’s WD_Folder_ID exists. If the Group \nrow lacks WD_Folder_ID, fix the Group first (admin). \n3. Wrong Group or Access selected\nDo not edit fields. Submit a support ticket to request admin correction. \n4. File replaced but old content shows\nClear browser cache/preview, or open the permalink in a new tab. WorkDrive previews \nmay take a moment to refresh. \n5. Duplicate SOP\nUse search before adding. If a duplicate exists, request admin to retire the extra record. \n6. Permission/API error\nYou may not have rights to upload to the Group’s WorkDrive folder, or the WorkDrive \nconnection is inactive. Contact an admin.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC. \n33F Robinsons Summit Center \n 6783 Ayala Avenue, Makati City 1226 \nMetro Manila \n \nwww.ececonsultinggroup.com \nFinal check: Verify in SOP Dashboard \nThe dashboard uses a sidebar-only list for SOP visibility. There are no filters or widgets \nto validate here. \n \nHome content (what you should see) \n●\nPage header: Home. \n●\nLeft sidebar: \n■\nSOP – Dashboard section with Home. \n■\nGroup sections are expandable/collapsible. \n●\nMain panel (Home): \n■\nA card per Group (e.g., ECETrack) showing the item(s) count. \n■\nEach card lists up to 10 SOP titles visible to the current user (General is \nalways visible; Support appears for Support/Admin users). \n■\nA VIEW ALL button sits at the bottom‑right of the card and navigates to \nthe full SOP list for that Group, scoped to the user’s access level. \n■\nIf a group has no SOPs yet, it won’t appear on the Home section.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC. \n33F Robinsons Summit Center \n 6783 Ayala Avenue, Makati City 1226 \nMetro Manila \n \nwww.ececonsultinggroup.com \nSidebar presence \n1. Open the SOP Dashboard in ECE Time Tracker. \n2. Check the sidebar: \n■\nConfirm the new SOP (file upload) appears by Title under the correct \nsection (General or Support). \n■\nSupport users can see the General section in addition to Support (per \npolicy). General-only users will not see Support. \n3. If the SOP title doesn’t appear in the sidebar: \n■\nRe‑check the record in All Sops (Title, Access, Group). \n■\nVerify the selected SOP Group exists and has a WD_Folder_ID in All Sop \nGroups. \n■\nSee Troubleshooting – SOP Group and Troubleshooting – SOP File \nUpload above. \nLink integrity & metadata \n●\nOn the dashboard, newly added SOPs display only as titles in the sidebar under \nGeneral and Support. \n●\nClicking a title should open the SOP file from Workdrive in SOP Dashboard. \n●\nAdditional metadata (timestamps, uploader, SOP Group/Access labels) are not \nshown in the sidebar list.\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC. \n33F Robinsons Summit Center \n 6783 Ayala Avenue, Makati City 1226 \nMetro Manila \n \nwww.ececonsultinggroup.com \nRequest help \n●\nSubmit a ticket if you’re experiencing an issue or have a suggestion: \nhttps://creatorapp.zoho.com/ececonsultinggroup/request-\nportal#Form:Zoho_Support_Ticketing \nChange log \n●\nv1.0 – Initial release of steps to create SOP Folder via All Sop Groups report.\n\n➕ Workforce RTA Logs\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Workforce Real-Time Analyst (RTA) \nWorkforce RTA Logs Process \n​\nWorkforce Logs SOP\n \n​\nListen to this tab\n​\nPurpose \nThe Workforce RTA Logs are designed to systematically capture and document all critical \noperational anomalies across the ECE organization. These logs serve as a communication and \ndocumentation tool to ensure management and operations are informed in real-time and can \ninitiate the appropriate response and long-term resolutions. \nThis SOP outlines the classification, documentation, and escalation process for all types of \nanomalies including service interruptions, behavioral issues, and performance alerts. \n \nScope \nThis SOP applies to all Real-Time Analysts (RTAs) and workforce staff responsible for monitoring \nintraday operations and maintaining accurate documentation of incidents affecting service level \ndelivery, employee productivity, and operational efficiency. \n \nWhen to Use the RTA Log \nUse the Workforce RTA Log when the following types of anomalies are observed: \n●​ A service level is being compromised (e.g., high ABN, low SLA) \n●​ Employee is violating standard behavior or compliance expectations \n●​ Technical/infrastructure issues affecting one or more employees/sites \n●​ Workflow interruptions due to system or process issues​\nTypes of RTA Logs \nEach entry in the RTA Logs must be categorized according to the scale of the impact: \n1.​ Site-Wide​\n Used when the situation affects the entire site or a large population across multiple \naccounts.​\n Example: Regional power outage or building-level internet disruption.​\n \n2.​ Account-Wide​\n For issues specific to a program or client account.​\n Example: A tool outage affecting only the XYZ client account or SLA drops on ABC \nprogram.​\n \n3.​ Employee (Specific)​\n Used for incidents involving a specific team member.​\n Example: Agent caught sleeping or an internet issue at a home-based workstation.​\n \n \nCategories and Sub-Categories \nMain Category \nSub-Category \nDescription \nService Level & Volume \nManagement \nSLA Escalation – P1 \n(85%) \nSLA dips below 85% for more than 15 \nminutes. \n \nSLA Escalation – P0 \n(60%) \nSLA dips below 60% in any 15-minute \ninterval. \n \nHigh Abandonment \nRate \nABN rate exceeds threshold per \naccount standards. \n \nUnderstaffing Alert \nReal-time headcount drops below \nrequired levels.\nOverstaffing Alert \nHeadcount significantly exceeds \nintraday requirement. \n \nQueue Surge / Low \nQueue Alert \nSudden rise or drop in volume that’s not \nforecasted. \nAgent Behavior & \nCompliance \nPost Abandonment \nAgent logs out or disconnects while on \na live contact. \n \nSleeping \nAgent inactive and unresponsive during \nlive monitoring. \n \nUnauthorized Use of \nCellphone \nAgent caught using phone during shift. \n \nUnscheduled Break / \nIdle Time \nTaking breaks beyond allowed or no \nactive state for prolonged period. \n \nExtended \nNon-Productive AUX \nStaying in non-productive states too \nlong (e.g., Break, Meeting). \n \nAccessing \nNon-Working Related \nSites \nVisiting websites that are not related to \nyour job or work responsibilities during \nworking hours or while using company \nequipment or networks. \n \nPossible Protraction / \nWork Delay \nDelay caused by internal or external \nblockers. \nTechnical & \nInfrastructure Issues \nPower Outage \nComplete loss of electricity affecting \nagent(s).\nInternet Outage \nAgent unable to connect due to \nconnectivity issues. \n \nTools Outage \nSpecific systems or platforms are down \n(e.g., Salesforce, Zendesk). \n \nLatency Issues \nApplication lagging or slowing down \nproductivity. \n \nHeadset / Device \nFailure \nHardware problems (broken mouse, \nheadset, keyboard). \nProcess & Work \nDisruptions \nPossible Protraction / \nWork Delay \nDelay caused by internal or external \nblockers. \n \nWorkforce System \nDowntime \nZoho, Genesys, WFM tools become \ninaccessible or malfunction. \n \nSystem Maintenance \nImpact \nKnown/planned maintenance that \ninterrupts work hours. \n \nStep-by-Step Logging Process \nStep 1: Identify the Situation​\n Once the anomaly is detected by the RTA or escalated to the team, assess whether it falls under \nthe scope of the Workforce RTA Log. \nStep 2: Determine the Log Type​\n Select the appropriate log type based on the scope of the issue (Site-Wide, Account-Wide, \nEmployee). \nStep 3: Select the Appropriate Category/Sub-Category​\n Based on the nature of the anomaly, assign it to the proper category and sub-category listed \nabove.\nStep 4: Fill Out the RTA Log Entry​\n Use the designated form to document the following: \n●​ Date and Time of the incident \n●​ Site and/or Account affected \n●​ Type of Log and Category/Sub-Category \n●​ Detailed description of the incident \n●​ Action taken by RTA or Operations \n●​ Escalation steps or contacts notified (e.g., TL, OM, IT, WFM) \n●​ Status: Resolved / Ongoing / Escalated​\n \nStep 5: Escalate If Necessary​\n Escalate incidents requiring urgent resolution (e.g., SLA P0 drops, tool outages) to Operations \nTeam. \nStep 6: Follow Up​\n Monitor if the issue persists. Provide updates in the same RTA Log entry until resolved. \n \nMitigations and Escalation Guidelines \n●​ For technical issues, immediately inform the IT Helpdesk or follow internal escalation \ntree.​\n \n●​ For agent compliance issues, escalate to TL or Operations via email or IM after logging.​\n \n●​ For volume or SLA alerts, coordinate with Operations to deploy available headcount, pull \nbreak queues, or reroute contacts.​\n \n●​ For site-wide events, confirm with Facilities and alert all impacted teams for contingency \n(e.g., reassign to other sites or split volume).​\n \n \nAccountability and Review \n●​ RTA Team Leads must audit the logs weekly to ensure completeness and resolution \ntracking.​\n \n●​ All logs must be submitted within 15 minutes from discovery of the event.​\n \n●​ Incomplete or late RTA logs may be subject to performance feedback or sanctioned \naccordingly for negligence.\nHow to Log Workforce RTA Logs (Site-Wide / Account-Wide) \nRefer to this SOP from Programming Team: \n \nWorkforce Logs SOP\nStep 1: Access the Workforce RTA Log System \n●​ Open your preferred web browser. \n●​ Go to the designated Workforce RTA Log Form. \n​\n \n \nStep 2: Select the Log Type \n●​ Choose either:​\n \n○​ Site-Wide – if the issue affects an entire site or multiple accounts. \n○​ Account-Wide – if the issue is isolated to a specific account or program.​\nStep 3: Identify the Affected Entity \n●​ For Site-Wide: Select the specific site name from the dropdown. \n●​ For Account-Wide: Select the account name or program affected.​\n \n \nStep 4: Choose the Correct Category and Sub-Category \n●​ Use the predefined categories:​\n \n○​ Service Level & Volume Management \n○​ Agent Behavior & Compliance \n○​ Technical & Infrastructure Issues \n○​ Process & Work Disruptions​\n \n●​ Then select the appropriate sub-category that best describes the situation.​\n \n \nStep 5: Provide Incident Details \nFill in the required fields with the following: \n●​ Date and Time of the Incident – When the issue occurred. \n●​ Site and/or Account Affected – Clearly indicate where the issue happened. \n●​ Type of Log – Confirm it is Site-Wide or Account-Wide. \n●​ Category / Sub-Category – Based on the nature of the incident. \n●​ Detailed Description – Briefly describe the situation, how it was discovered, what was \nobserved, and any relevant context. \n●​ Action Taken by RTA or Operations – Note any immediate steps, communication, \nescalation, or resolution attempts. \n●​ Status – Choose one:​\n \n○​ Resolved – if fully addressed \n○​ Ongoing – if still being monitored or partially resolved \n○​ Escalated – if forwarded to IT, Ops, or Management for action​\n \n \nStep 6: Submit and Monitor \n●​ Click Submit or Save once all fields are filled out. \n●​ Continue monitoring the situation even after logging. \n●​ If the issue persists or changes status, update the same log entry with the new \ndevelopments until fully resolved.​\nHow to Log Workforce RTA Logs (Employee-Specific) \n \nStep 1: Access the Workforce RTA Log System \n●​ Open your preferred web browser. \n●​ Go to the designated Workforce RTA Log Form.​\n \n \nStep 2: Select Type of Log \n●​ Choose \"Employee-Specific\" as the type of log entry.​\n \n \nStep 3: Identify the Employee \n●​ Select the Employee’s Name from the dropdown or input field.​\n \n●​ Select the Site and Account where the employee is assigned.​\n \n \nStep 4: Choose the Appropriate Category and Sub-Category \nUnder Agent Behavior & Compliance, select the relevant sub-category:\n●​ Post Abandonment – Agent disconnected/logged out during active contact.​\n \n●​ Sleeping – Agent inactive and unresponsive.​\n \n●​ Unauthorized Use of Cellphone – Agent caught using a phone while on duty.​\n \n●​ Unscheduled Break/Idle Time – Agent took excessive or unscheduled breaks.​\n \n●​ Extended Non-Productive AUX – Agent stayed too long in non-productive states, \nincluding:​\n \n○​ Prolonged After Call Work (ACW) \n○​ Prolonged Average Handle Time (AHT) \n○​ Unauthorized usage of offline AUX \n○​ Logging out without approval \n○​ Any of the above that negatively affected the SLA​\n \n \nStep 5: Fill in the Incident Details \nProvide the following information: \n●​ Date and Time of the Incident – When it happened. \n●​ Category/Sub-Category – Based on the agent’s behavior. \n●​ Detailed Description – Include what was observed or reported, how it was confirmed \n(screenshots, chat logs, etc.), and any relevant patterns of behavior.​\n \n \nStep 6: Upload Supporting Documents \n●​ Upload any evidence to support the log:​\n \n○​ Screenshots \n○​ Chat or system logs \n○​ AUX reports​\n \n●​ Recommendation: Attach an NTE/NOD recommendation or coaching documentation if \napplicable.​\n \n \nStep 7: Submit the Log Entry \n●​ Double-check all fields. \n●​ Click Submit or Save to log the report.\nStep 8: Monitoring and Operations Action \n●​ Once submitted, the Operations Team (TL, STL, Managers) will receive an automated \nemail notification about the RTA log.​\n \n●​ The Ops Team must respond by issuing an:​\n \n○​ NTE (Notice to Explain) or NOD (Notice of Disciplinary Action) \n○​ Logging a coaching session \nOnce submitted, the Operations Team (TL, STL, Managers) will receive an email alert with \nthe report. \nWithin the email/system, they can: \nClick “NTE/NOD” to issue a disciplinary citation. \nClick “Coaching” to log a coaching form.​\n​\n \n \n​\n \nAccountability: \n❖​ The Immediate Supervisor (e.g., TL) is solely responsible for ensuring the incident \nis addressed. \n❖​ If the immediate supervisor is unavailable, responsibility follows the hierarchy (STL, \nthen Manager). \n❖​ The Immediate Supervisor is expected to act within 5 calendar days from the date \nthe RTA log was submitted. \n❖​ Failure to act within 5 days will result in the Immediate Supervisor being held \naccountable and cited for negligence.​\n \n●​ RTAs will monitor if the action has been completed and document the follow-up on the \nsame entry if needed.\n✅ WFM Escalation Workflow\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Workforce Real-Time Analyst (RTA) \n📊 Workforce RTA Escalation Workflow \n \n1. Issue Identification & Log Entry \n●​ RTA identifies SLA failure, AHOD instance, or any real-time operational concern. \n●​ RTA documents the issue in the Zoho Creator -  ECETrack - Workforce RTA Logs \nwith complete details (timestamp, queue, agent, impact, actions taken).​\n \n \n2. Initial Notification \n●​ RTA sends the alert to the Support Operations Team through the designated \nchannel (Slack, Teams, email, or ticketing system). \n●​ Timestamp is recorded in the Workforce RTA Log.​\n \n \n3. Wait for Acknowledgement \n●​ Standard waiting period: 5–10 minutes depending on urgency. \n●​ If no acknowledgement is received, proceed to escalation.​\n \n \n4. First Escalation – Senior Operations Leadership \nIf no acknowledgement is received from the Support Operations Team within the \nstandard response window (5–10 minutes):\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Workforce Real-Time Analyst (RTA) \n📊 Workforce RTA Escalation Workflow \n \nStep 1: Escalate to Senior Operations Leadership \n●​ Escalation Recipients:​\n \n1.​ Senior Team Leader \n2.​ Workforce RTA Manager \n3.​ Operations Manager​\n \n●​ Purpose:​\n Ensure timely visibility and intervention for SLA failures, queue issues, or \noperational disruptions.​\n \nStep 2: Communication Channels \n●​ Zoho Cliq:​\n Send a direct message immediately outlining:​\n \n○​ Issue summary \n○​ Queue impacted \n○​ Agents affected \n○​ Actions already taken \n○​ Requested response time​\n \n●​ Phone Call:​\n If no response via Cliq within 5 minutes, call directly using the updated contact \nnumbers of each recipient. Include:​\n \n○​ Clear description of the issue \n○​ Urgency level \n○​ Required action\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Workforce Real-Time Analyst (RTA) \n📊 Workforce RTA Escalation Workflow \n \n○​ Any dependencies affecting resolution​\n \nStep 3: Documentation \n●​ Record all escalation attempts in the RTA Log including:​\n \n○​ Date and time of escalation \n○​ Channel used (Cliq or Phone) \n○​ Name of person contacted \n○​ Response received (if any) \n○​ Actions taken or next steps​\n \nStep 4: Follow-up \n●​ Continue monitoring until acknowledgement or resolution is received.​\n \n●​ If the senior leadership team still does not respond, escalate immediately to the \nExecutive Team following the documented escalation procedure. \n \n \n5. Second Escalation – Executive Team \nIf senior management also does not acknowledge or action the issue within the \nescalation window: \n➡️ Escalate to the Executive Leadership Team through email or Cliq: \n1.​ Michael Baldwin – VP for Operations\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Workforce Real-Time Analyst (RTA) \n📊 Workforce RTA Escalation Workflow \n \n2.​ Breana Odekirk – Director of Operations \n3.​ Chelsea Sidwell – Director of Implementation \n4.​ Jennifer Carabeo – Executive Director \n5.​ Marta Rub – VP of Finance \n6.​ Chris Eisdorfer – CEO​\n \nIf senior management (Senior Team Leader, Workforce RTA Manager, Operations \nManager) does not acknowledge or take action within the escalation window: \nEscalation Recipients \n●​ Michael Baldwin – VP for Operations \n●​ Breana Odekirk – Director of Operations \n●​ Chelsea Sidwell – Director of Implementation \n●​ Jennifer Carabeo – Executive Director \n●​ Marta Rub – VP of Finance \n●​ Chris Eisdorfer – CEO​\n \nRequired Escalation Actions \nFollow these steps to ensure proper notification: \n1.​ Send a Zoho Cliq Message​\n \n○​ Include issue summary, queue impacted, agents affected, actions taken, \nand urgency.​\n \n2.​ Send an Email​\n \n○​ Provide the same information as above, attach relevant RTA logs if needed.​\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Workforce Real-Time Analyst (RTA) \n📊 Workforce RTA Escalation Workflow \n \n3.​ Call via Zoho Cliq​\n \n○​ Attempt direct communication if no response via message or email.​\n \n4.​ Call via Phone​\n \n○​ Use updated executive contact numbers to ensure immediate \nacknowledgement.​\n \nDocumentation \n - Use this for incident report. \nWFM SLA Failure Escalation Ticket Template\n●​ Include the following in the escalation:​\n \n○​ Complete RTA Log \n○​ Summary of escalation attempts (all channels and timestamps) \n○​ Business impact \n○​ Required action (urgent/critical)​\n \n \n6. Resolution & Closure \nOnce the issue is acknowledged and addressed: \n1.​ Update the RTA Log​\n \n○​ Action taken \n○​ Time resolved \n○​ Team/leader who resolved the issue​\nECENTERPRISES GROUP MANILA INC  \n33F Robinsons Summit Center, 6783 Ayala Avenue Makati City, 1200  \nMetro Manila, 1200, Philippines \nhttps://www.ececonsultinggroup.com/  \n \nStandard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Workforce Real-Time Analyst (RTA) \n📊 Workforce RTA Escalation Workflow \n \n2.​ Close the Case​\n \n○​ Send a brief summary to the operations chan